{"id": "107", "question": "what is the difference between the leeward and windward islands?", "gt": "The Windward and Leeward Islands are part of the Lesser Antilles of the Caribbean Sea. The Windward Islands are in the southeast and are exposed to the northeast trade winds, hence they receive more rain and are wetter. On the other hand, the Leeward Islands are located in the northwest and are away from the wind, making them drier.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the Windward Islands are exposed to the northeast trade winds and are wetter, receiving more rain, while the Leeward Islands are away from the wind and are drier. The Windward Islands are the southeastern islands of the Lesser Antilles, whereas the Leeward Islands are the northwestern islands. The Windward side of a mountain is closer to the ocean and gets more rain, while the Leeward side is farther from the shore and is drier.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the Windward Islands are exposed to the northeast trade winds and are wetter, receiving more rain, while the Leeward Islands are away from the wind and are drier. The Windward Islands are the southeastern islands of the Lesser Antilles, whereas the Leeward Islands are the northwestern islands. The Windward side of a mountain is closer to the ocean and gets more rain, while the Leeward side is farther from the shore and is drier.", "time_sec": 17.52, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 22087, 1606, 22235, 525, 14900, 311, 279, 40829, 6559, 28492, 323, 525, 14401, 465, 11, 12308, 803, 11174, 11, 1393, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 525, 3123, 504, 279, 9956, 323, 525, 294, 7253, 13, 576, 22087, 1606, 22235, 525, 279, 82109, 29000, 315, 279, 13907, 6755, 30255, 11, 19853, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 525, 279, 10200, 30282, 29000, 13, 576, 22087, 1606, 3108, 315, 264, 16301, 374, 12128, 311, 279, 17951, 323, 5221, 803, 11174, 11, 1393, 279, 1967, 24035, 3108, 374, 42626, 504, 279, 30184, 323, 374, 294, 7253, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0017, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.01, -0.4029, -0.0, -0.0007, -0.0063, -0.2562, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.3189, -0.0, -0.0, -0.4819, -0.3646, -0.7587, -0.0, -0.6195, -0.0671, -0.0, -0.0298, -0.8897, -0.3554, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0007, -0.3331, -0.0, -0.1304, -0.0275, -0.233, -0.0315, -0.0488, 0.0, -0.2127, -0.0277, -0.0539, -0.0, -0.0067, -0.0822, -0.6671, -0.0029, -0.0093, -0.05, -0.0, -0.314, -0.0, -0.0, -0.9549, -0.4228, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0029, -0.0258, -0.0, -0.0, -0.1145, -0.3572, -0.3953, -0.9106, -0.0, -0.4894, -0.4926, -0.5604, -0.0793, -0.7807, -0.2466, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0013, -0.08, -0.8348, -0.0023, -0.5119, -0.0175, -0.0825, -0.0, -0.127, -0.0, -0.0054, -0.012, -0.0271, -0.0025, -0.4746, -0.1637, -0.0301, -0.1737, -0.1139, 0.0, -0.4003, -0.136], "cumulative_logprob": -15.8265, "norm_logp": -0.1599, "input_len": 500, "output_tokens": 99, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 51.95, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "113", "question": "how are water shares transferred", "gt": "To transfer water shares, the seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of it. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer. After these steps, a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner. If the original certificate is lost, an additional fee of $75.00 must be paid when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form, which is furnished by the Company and must be signed and notarized.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, water shares are transferred by following these steps: 1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate. 2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership. 3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer. 4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record. Additionally, if the certificate is lost, an additional $75.00 fee is required to file a Lost Certificate Affidavit form, which must be signed and notarized.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, water shares are transferred by following these steps: 1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate. 2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership. 3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer. 4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record. Additionally, if the certificate is lost, an additional $75.00 fee is required to file a Lost Certificate Affidavit form, which must be signed and notarized.", "time_sec": 22.401, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 3015, 13248, 525, 22409, 553, 2701, 1493, 7354, 25, 220,