{"id": "125", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the process of building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site with compacted gravel, cutting and setting the 4 x 4 skids, cutting and assembling the floor with 2 x 6 rim joists and joists, anchoring the frame to the skids, attaching tongue-and-groove plywood flooring, constructing the walls separately, and raising them onto the frame.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Cut two 4x4 skids to 70 2/4 inches and set them level. Cut two 2x6 rim joists to 7 3/4 inches and six joists to 44 3/4 inches, then assemble the floor frame and set it on the skids. Check for square and anchor the frame using four joist clip angles. Alternatively, cut two pressure-treated 4x4s to 6 feet for skids, position the frame, toenail floor joists to skids, and attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring. Walls are built separately and raised onto the frame. The shed dimensions can be 6 feet by 4 feet or expanded in 2 or 4-foot increments.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Cut two 4x4 skids to 70 2/4 inches and set them level. Cut two 2x6 rim joists to 7 3/4 inches and six joists to 44 3/4 inches, then assemble the floor frame and set it on the skids. Check for square and anchor the frame using four joist clip angles. Alternatively, cut two pressure-treated 4x4s to 6 feet for skids, position the frame, toenail floor joists to skids, and attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring. Walls are built separately and raised onto the frame. The shed dimensions can be 6 feet by 4 feet or expanded in 2 or 4-foot increments.", "time_sec": 32.632, "rec