{"id": "272", "question": "earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy", "gt": "The earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy include mood swings, dizziness, bloating, spotting, cramping, nausea, and vomiting.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy include a missed period, bloating, spotting, cramping, mood swings due to hormonal changes, dizziness from blood vessel dilation and dropped blood pressure, and nausea or vomiting. Around half of all pregnant women experience nausea and vomiting, with symptoms typically starting around six weeks after the last period. Some women may also feel unusually emotional or weepy in early pregnancy.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy include a missed period, bloating, spotting, cramping, mood swings due to hormonal changes, dizziness from blood vessel dilation and dropped blood pressure, and nausea or vomiting. Around half of all pregnant women experience nausea and vomiting, with symptoms typically starting around six weeks after the last period. Some women may also feel unusually emotional or weepy in early pregnancy.", "time_sec": 15.623, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 29658, 11929, 323, 13495, 315, 19636, 2924, 264, 13628, 4168, 11, 14211, 1095, 11, 89219, 11, 1560, 30457, 11, 19671, 56790, 4152, 311, 73118, 4344, 11, 294, 96645, 504, 6543, 26182, 74278, 323, 12226, 6543, 7262, 11, 323, 60780, 476, 62471, 13, 32816, 4279, 315, 678, 20280, 3198, 3139, 60780, 323, 62471, 11, 448, 13495, 11136, 5916, 2163, 4743, 5555, 1283, 279, 1537, 4168, 13, 4329, 3198, 1231, 1083, 2666, 56799, 14269, 476, 582, 70548, 304, 4124, 19636, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0036, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.1251, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0486, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.2423, -0.3985, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0014, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.062, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0261, -0.0001, -0.3839, -0.0, -0.0304, -0.0063, -0.0192, -0.0097, 0.0, -0.1644, -0.3605, -0.0177, -0.0, -0.0028, -0.8431, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0283, -0.0011, -0.7063, -0.0002, -0.5495, -0.7278, -0.0211, -0.0, -0.3872, -0.0009, -0.0, -0.0118, -0.0017, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.0922, -0.6332, -0.315, -0.5267, -0.1604, -0.0703, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0182, -0.0, -0.062, -0.6961, -0.631, -0.0145, -0.4338, -0.7842, -1.0181, -0.058, -0.0003, -0.1202, -0.0503, -0.0, -1.3575, -0.0233, -0.0028, -0.184, -0.0703], "cumulative_logprob": -12.5057, "norm_logp": -0.1437, "input_len": 474, "output_tokens": 87, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 38.24, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "283", "question": "difference between an adverb clause and an adjective clause", "gt": "Based on the given passages, an adverb clause modifies a verb, adjective or another adverb, while an adjective clause modifies a noun or pronoun.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, an adverb clause is a dependent clause that modifies a verb, adjective, or another adverb, usually modifying the verb, and is introduced by subordinate conjunctions such as after, although, as, because, if, since, until, when, where, and while. In contrast, an adjective clause modifies a noun or pronoun and is introduced by a relative pronoun (who, whose, whom, which, that) or a subordinate conjunction (when, where). While both are dependent clauses, their functions differ: adverb clauses modify verbs or adjectives, whereas adjective clauses modify nouns or pronouns.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, an adverb clause is a dependent clause that modifies a verb, adjective, or another adverb, usually modifying the verb, and is introduced by subordinate conjunctions such as after, although, as, because, if, since, until, when, where, and while. In contrast, an adjective clause modifies a noun or pronoun and is introduced by a relative pronoun (who, whose, whom, which, that) or a subordinate conjunction (when, where). While both are dependent clauses, their functions differ: adverb clauses modify verbs or adjectives, whereas adjective clauses modify nouns or pronouns.", "time_sec": 22.784, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 458, 993, 22328, 21647, 374, 264, 17749, 21647, 429, 82949, 264, 18607, 11, 84492, 11, 476, 2441, 993, 22328, 11, 5990, 46041, 279, 18607, 11, 323, 374, 11523, 553, 78163, 31446, 82, 1741, 438, 1283, 11, 7892, 11, 438, 11, 1576, 11, 421, 11, 2474, 11, 3080, 11, 979, 11, 1380, 11, 323, 1393, 13, 758, 12872, 11, 458, 84