{"id": "338", "question": "how to make ribs", "gt": "To make ribs, start by removing the membrane from the bottom of the ribs with a knife. Place the ribs in a resealable bag and add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover them. Afterwards, line a baking pan with heavy duty foil. Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer for heat circulation on all sides. Mix mustard and liquid smoke, if using, and brush the ribs on both sides. Sprinkle the ribs with a dry rub and pat gently to make sure it adheres to the meat. To grill the ribs, heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium and remove the ribs from the foil. Place them meaty-side up on the grill and brush them with some of the sauce. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook for another 5 minutes. Continue this process until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through with grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to make ribs, first remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs using a knife to start it near the narrow end and pull it off in one piece. Then, lay the ribs on a rack in a single layer to allow heat circulation on all sides. Season the ribs by mixing mustard and liquid smoke (if using) and brushing both sides, then sprinkle with a dry rub and pat gently to adhere. For grilling, heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F), place the ribs meaty-side up, brush with sauce, cover, and cook for 5 minutes. Flip, brush again, and cook another 5 minutes. Continue flipping and brushing every 5 minutes until the sauce thickens and ribs are heated through with grill marks, totaling 20 minutes. For oven cooking, place ribs in a resealable bag with enough BBQ sauce to cover, and line a baking pan with heavy-duty foil to make a tent.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to make ribs, first remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs using a knife to start it near the narrow end and pull it off in one piece. Then, lay the ribs on a rack in a single layer to allow heat circulation on all sides. Season the ribs by mixing mustard and liquid smoke (if using) and brushing both sides, then sprinkle with a dry rub and pat gently to adhere. For grilling, heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F), place the ribs meaty-side up, brush with sauce, cover, and cook for 5 minutes. Flip, brush again, and cook another 5 minutes. Continue flipping and brushing every 5 minutes until the sauce thickens and ribs are heated through with grill marks, totaling 20 minutes. For oven cooking, place ribs in a resealable bag with enough BBQ sauce to cover, and line a baking pan with heavy-duty foil to make a tent.", "time_sec": 35.859, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1281, 55149, 11, 1156, 4057, 279, 38554, 504, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 55149, 1667, 264, 21430, 311, 1191, 432, 3143, 279, 15026, 835, 323, 6815, 432, 1007, 304, 825, 6573, 13, 5005, 11, 10962, 279, 55149, 389, 264, 29659, 304, 264, 3175, 6193, 311, 2138, 8628, 34755, 389, 678, 11067, 13, 14263, 279, 55149, 553, 26792, 64307, 323, 14473, 16205, 320, 333, 1667, 8, 323, 76726, 2176, 11067, 11, 1221, 84847, 448, 264, 9058, 10273, 323, 3272, 29273, 311, 48453, 13, 1752, 1081, 9400, 11, 8628, 264, 6819, 476, 60103, 39058, 311, 11051, 320, 18, 20, 15, 58472, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 701, 1992, 279, 55149, 13041, 88, 24067, 705, 11, 15625, 448, 19187, 11, 3421, 11, 323, 4296, 369, 220, 20, 4420, 13, 40284, 11, 15625, 1549, 11, 323, 4296, 2441, 220, 20, 4420, 13, 15003, 64661, 323, 76726, 1449, 220, 20, 4420, 3080, 279, 19187, 12045, 724, 323, 55149, 525, 31713, 1526, 448, 39058, 15423, 11, 81123, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 13, 1752, 23387, 17233, 11, 1992, 55149, 304, 264, 312, 325, 278, 480, 8968, 448, 3322, 45277, 19187, 311, 3421, 11, 323, 1555, 264, 27815, 7215, 448, 8811, 545