{"id": "495", "question": "salary exchange pension contributions", "gt": "Salary exchange pension contributions, also known as salary sacrifice, is a method where an employee agrees to give up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment paid by their employer. This can allow both employers and employees to save money. The salary that is waived under the salary exchange is equal to the value of the regular pension contribution made. For example, it could be 7.5% or 9% of the pay, depending on the pension scheme. The employer then pays a corresponding amount into the relevant pension scheme.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, salary exchange pension contributions involve an employee agreeing to give up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment made by their employer. This arrangement allows both employers and employees to save money, as employers pay lower National Insurance Contributions (NICs) due to the reduced salary payments. Salary exchange is also referred to as salary sacrifice and typically involves non-cash benefits such as pension contributions. For example, at the University, the waived salary amount matches the employee's regular pension contribution—7.5% of pay for USS members effective from 1 October 2011 and 9% for USPAS members effective from 1 August 2011—while the University contributes an equivalent amount into the relevant pension scheme.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, salary exchange pension contributions involve an employee agreeing to give up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment made by their employer. This arrangement allows both employers and employees to save money, as employers pay lower National Insurance Contributions (NICs) due to the reduced salary payments. Salary exchange is also referred to as salary sacrifice and typically involves non-cash benefits such as pension contributions. For example, at the University, the waived salary amount matches the employee's regular pension contribution—7.5% of pay for USS members effective from 1 October 2011 and 9% for USPAS members effective from 1 August 2011—while the University contributes an equivalent amount into the relevant pension scheme.", "time_sec": 27.246, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 16107, 9289, 27681, 19026, 21058, 458, 9364, 38327, 311, 2968, 705, 949, 315, 862, 16107, 476, 12037, 304, 9289, 369, 264, 27681, 8160, 1865, 553, 862, 19136, 13, 1096, 26112, 6147, 2176, 22426, 323, 8256, 311, 3581, 3220, 11, 438, 22426, 2291, 4722, 5055, 21674, 96004, 320, 44947, 82, 8, 4152, 311, 279, 11046, 16107, 14173, 13, 41758, 9289, 374, 1083, 13862, 311, 438, 16107, 27136, 323, 11136, 17601, 2477, 1786, 988, 7567, 1741, 438, 27681, 19026, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 518, 279, 3822, 11, 279, 81482, 16107, 3311, 9071, 279, 9364, 594, 5792, 27681, 18527, 2293, 22, 13, 20, 4, 315, 2291, 369, 38508, 3613, 7373, 504, 220, 16, 6527, 220, 17, 15, 16, 16, 323, 220, 24, 4, 369, 2274, 47, 1911, 3613, 7373, 504, 220, 16, 6156, 220, 17, 15, 16, 16, 2293, 3472, 279, 3822, 42972, 458, 13578, 3311, 1119, 279, 9760, 27681, 12859, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0076, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.1189, -0.0, -0.1201, -0.0207, -0.0027, -0.2354, -0.0, -0.1454, -0.0, -0.0111, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.4288, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.4742, -0.0, -0.0289, -0.0267, -0.1603, -0.2689, -0.0007, -0.0015, -0.0, -0.1183, -0.0166, -0.0566, -0.6064, -0.2479, -0.1584, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0372, -0.0251, -0.3892, -0.1844, -0.0229, -0.0491, -0.0014, -0.0156, -0.0, -0.0087, -0.0036, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0023, -0.0431, -0.0, -0.6578, -0.044, -0.0885, -0.5262, -0.0177, -1.0749, -0.0005, -0.3879, -0.0313, -0.4005, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0233, -0.0, -0.4139, -1.0258, -0.5746, -1.0312, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.7303, -0.0, -0.1261, -0.0004, -0.0035, -0.1264, 