{"id": "103", "question": "how the body systems work together", "gt": "The various systems in the human body work together to ensure its normal functioning. For instance, the urinary system works with all other systems to clean the blood by removing waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. This includes organs like the kidneys and lower intestines. Similarly, the respiratory system also collaborates with all other systems to provide oxygen to all body parts and remove carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. The respiratory system comprises the nose, larynx, trachea, and lungs.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, body systems work together to maintain normal functioning. The urinary system cleans waste from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system supplies oxygen to all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. Both systems collaborate with others to ensure proper bodily function.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, body systems work together to maintain normal functioning. The urinary system cleans waste from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system supplies oxygen to all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. Both systems collaborate with others to ensure proper bodily function.", "time_sec": 13.818, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 311, 10306, 4622, 30201, 13, 576, 71635, 1849, 34194, 12291, 504, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 1