{"id": "108", "question": "what is the difference between the leeward and windward islands?", "gt": "The Windward Islands are exposed to the wind of the northeast trade winds and are located on the southeastern side of the Caribbean Sea. The Leeward Islands, on the other hand, are located on the northwestern side of the Lesser Antilles and are away from the wind. The windward side receives more rain and is wetter, while the leeward side is drier but still receives some rain.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the Windward Islands are exposed to the northeast trade winds and are wetter, receiving more rain, while the Leeward Islands are away from the wind and are drier. The Windward Islands are the southeastern islands of the Lesser Antilles, whereas the Leeward Islands are the northwestern islands. The Windward side of a mountain is closer to the ocean and gets more rain, while the Leeward side is farther from the shore and is drier.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the Windward Islands are exposed to the northeast trade winds and are wetter, receiving more rain, while the Leeward Islands are away from the wind and are drier. The Windward Islands are the southeastern islands of the Lesser Antilles, whereas the Leeward Islands are the northwestern islands. The Windward side of a mountain is closer to the ocean and gets more rain, while the Leeward side is farther from the shore and is drier.", "time_sec": 17.157, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 22087, 1606, 22235, 525, 14900, 311, 279, 40829, 6559, 28492, 323, 525, 14401, 465, 11, 12308, 803, 11174, 11, 1393, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 525, 3123, 504, 279, 9956, 323, 525, 294, 7253, 13, 576, 22087, 1606, 22235, 525, 279, 82109, 29000, 315, 279, 13907, 6755, 30255, 11, 19853, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 525, 279, 10200, 30282, 29000, 13, 576, 22087, 16