{"id": "114", "question": "how are water shares transferred", "gt": "Water shares are transferred by following a set of steps. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate and sign the back of the certificate. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer. After completing these steps, a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, water shares are transferred by following these steps: 1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate. 2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership. 3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer. 4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record. Additionally, if the certificate is lost, an additional $75.00 fee is required to file a Lost Certificate Affidavit form, which must be signed and notarized.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, water shares are transferred by following these steps: 1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate. 2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership. 3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer. 4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record. Additionally, if the certificate is lost, an additional $75.00 fee is required to file a Lost Certificate Affidavit form, which must be signed and notarized.", "time_sec": 22.166, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 3015, 13248, 525, 22409, 553, 2701, 1493, 7354, 25, 220, 16, 13, 576, 22856, 1969, 470, 279, 9959, 12648, 31402, 12607, 311, 1105, 323, 1841, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 15748, 13, 220, 17, 13, 576, 501, 6372, 315, 279, 3343, 1969, 3410, 