{"id": "233", "question": "average weather sausalito", "gt": "The highest monthly average temperature in Sausalito is 58 degrees in September and the lowest is 50 degrees in December. The city gets 34 inches of rain per year, with the most precipitation occurring in January. Snowfall is non-existent. On average, there are 256 sunny days per year. The July high is around 69 degrees and the January low is 43. The air quality index is 13% better than the national average, however, the pollution index is 61% worse.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, Sausalito has an average yearly precipitation of 34 inches, with 56 days of measurable precipitation annually. The city receives 256 sunny days per year. The average temperature in July is around 69 degrees, while the January low is 43 degrees. The highest monthly average temperature occurs in September at 58 degrees, and the lowest monthly average temperature is in December at 50 degrees. Sausalito has no snowfall, with an average of 0 inches annually. The air quality index is 13% better than the national average, but the pollution index is 61% worse. Sausalito's comfort index is 84 out of 100, significantly higher than the US average of 54, indicating a more comfortable climate year-round.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, Sausalito has an average yearly precipitation of 34 inches, with 56 days of measurable precipitation annually. The city receives 256 sunny days per year. The average temperature in July is around 69 degrees, while the January low is 43 degrees. The highest monthly average temperature occurs in September at 58 degrees, and the lowest monthly average temperature is in December at 50 degrees. Sausalito has no snowfall, with an average of 0 inches annually. The air quality index is 13% better than the national average, but the pollution index is 61% worse. Sausalito's comfort index 