{"id": "304", "question": "what causes watermelons to explode", "gt": "Watermelons can explode due to external pressure, such as when a bunch of rubber bands are placed around the middle of the watermelon, causing potential energy to build up and eventually cause the watermelon to explode. Another cause of watermelon explosions is the buildup of gas inside the watermelon due to rotting. This increases the internal pressure and when the skin of the watermelon can no longer hold the gas inside, it will explode.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, watermelons explode due to the buildup of gas inside them as they rot. This gas increases the internal pressure, and when the pressure becomes too high for the watermelon's skin to contain, it causes the watermelon to explode.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, watermelons explode due to the buildup of gas inside them as they rot. This gas increases the internal pressure, and when the pressure becomes too high for the watermelon's skin to contain, it causes the watermelon to explode.", "time_sec": 10.087, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 3015, 27127, 2382, 15758, 4152, 311, 279, 85665, 315, 6819, 4766, 1105, 438, 807, 5749, 13, 1096, 6819, 12703, 279, 5306, 7262, 11, 323, 979, 279, 7262, 9044, 2238, 1550, 369, 279, 3015, 71118, 594, 6787, 311, 6644, 11, 432, 11137, 279, 3015, 71118, 311, 15758, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0028, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0009, -0.0409, 0.0, -0.3025, -0.0964, -0.0, -0.0277, -0.2677, -0.7553, -0.5219, -0.0388, -0.0044, -0.0051, -0.2648, -0.0235, -0.148, -0.1027, -0.062, -0.0, -0.4892, -0.015, -0.018, -0.0001, -0.6089, -0.3926, -0.0013, -0.8849, -0.1571, -0.0, -0.027, -0.0, -0.0396, -0.0044, -0.0, -0.2254, -0.0126, -0.6329, -1.0878, -0.0161, -0.0238, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0935, -0.5794, -0.5434], "cumulative_logprob": -8.5189, "norm_logp": -0.1578, "input_len": 487, "output_tokens": 54, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.54, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "321", "question": "what is the effect of carbon footprint", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the effect of carbon footprint is to measure the environmental impact of an individual's lifestyle and daily activities, specifically the amount of greenhouse gases produced, such as carbon dioxide, as a result of those activities. The carbon footprint is typically measured in tons of CO2 released into the atmosphere. The passages also mention that reducing one's carbon footprint can have a significant impact on the environment, even with seemingly small changes. Additionally, the average carbon footprint is mentioned to be around 6 tons per year, with a higher amount in the US due to automobile emissions.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the effect of carbon footprint is to measure the environmental impact of human activities by quantifying the amount of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases produced. It indicates how lifestyle choices contribute to climate change and environmental degradation. For example, the average person's carbon footprint is 6 tons per year globally, while in the U.S. it is 20 tons per year, with a significant portion coming from automobile emissions. Activities like heating homes, eating food such as cheeseburgers, and driving cars all contribute to this footprint, showing how daily actions affect the environment.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the effect of carbon footprint is to measure the environmental impact of human activities by quantifying the amount of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases produced. It indicates how lifestyle choices contribute to climate change and environmental degradation. For example, the average person's carbon footprint is 6 tons per year globally, while in the U.S. it is 20 tons per year, with a significant portion coming from automobile emissions. Activities like heating homes, eating food such as cheeseburgers, and driving cars all contribute to this footprint, showing how daily actions affect the environment.", "time_sec": 20.461, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 2456, 315, 12499, 42872, 374, 311, 6629, 279, 12158, 5421, 315, 3738, 7488, 553, 10272, 7766, 279, 3311, 315, 12499, 39489, 323, 1008, 36547, 44512, 8947, 13, 1084, 14807, 1246, 18899, 11454, 16792, 311, 9977, 2297, 323, 12158, 52468, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 5461, 1697, 594, 12499, 42872, 374, 220, 21, 19608, 817, 1042, 30450, 11, 1393, 304, 279, 547, 808, 13, 432, 374, 220, 17, 15, 19608, 817, 1042, 11, 448, 264, 5089, 13348, 5001, 504, 34428, 20143, 13, 43282, 1075, 23579, 10415, 11, 12182, 3607, 1741, 438, 17163, 10269, 388, 11, 323, 9842, 9331, 678, 16792, 311, 419, 42872, 11, 9027, 1246, 7298, 6168, 7802, 279, 4573, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0026, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.2237, -0.2032, -0.0, -0.3184, -0.0001, -0.0142, -1.0722, -0.0022, -0.0005, -0.0093, -0.0, -0.0172, -0.6289, -0.0152, -0.8721, -0.4166, -0.0, -0.0016, -0.0806, -0.0, -0.3869, -0.0, -0.0041, -0.0008, -0.0, -0.0, -0.1626, -0.1478, -0.7469, -0.968, -0.5258, -0.5907, -0.0061, -1.0172, -0.0, -0.6198, -0.0307, -0.7076, -0.238, -0.0478, -0.079, -0.9212, -0.2268, -0.0, -1.3186, -0.032, -1.2851, -1.0959, -0.1582, -0.0018, -0.0179, -0.0383, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.3673, -0.0, -0.2558, -0.0243, -0.7897, -0.1569, -0.0, -0.0061, -0.0, -0.3489, -0.0005, -0.2353, -0.0631, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0, -0.7779, -0.0001, -0.2445, -0.0322, -1.431, -0.2242, -0.0203, -0.6248, -0.0, -0.7029, -0.0833, -0.4, -0.9514, -0.5773, -0.4912, -0.0078, -0.5316, -0.2341, -0.7929, -0.7504, -0.0, -0.5207, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0233, -0.0083, -0.1002, -0.0723, -0.0895, -0.6983, -0.0276, -1.1757, -0.1128, -0.6022, -0.7624, -0.5704, -0.5658, -0.9745, -1.1432, -0.0164, -0.2943, -0.0746, -0.156], "cumulative_logprob": -34.3692, "norm_logp": -0.2888, "input_len": 582, "output_tokens": 119, "eval