{"id": "478", "question": "change of address u.s. postal service", "gt": "Passage 3 provides information on how to change your address with the U.S. Postal Service. You can visit their website, call the USPS Call Center, or fill out and submit a form at a U.S. Post Office.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, you can change your address with the U.S. Postal Service in multiple ways. First, you can use the online service at https://moversguide.usps.com/, which allows you to change your address in as little as 1 minute and includes identity validation via a $1 charge to your credit or debit card. Second, you can call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777). Third, you can fill out and submit PS Form 3575 either in person at any U.S. Post Office, by mail to any Post Office, or by giving it to a Postal Mail Carrier. Additionally, the service allows you to notify up to 100 organizations besides USPS and uses encryption to secure your data.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, you can change your address with the U.S. Postal Service in multiple ways. First, you can use the online service at https://moversguide.usps.com/, which allows you to change your address in as little as 1 minute and includes identity validation via a $1 charge to your credit or debit card. Second, you can call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777). Third, you can fill out and submit PS Form 3575 either in person at any U.S. Post Office, by mail to any Post Office, or by giving it to a Postal Mail Carrier. Additionally, the service allows you to notify up to 100 organizations besides USPS and uses encryption to secure your data.", "time_sec": 29.466, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 498, 646, 2297, 697, 2621, 448, 279, 547, 808, 13, 54217, 5362, 304, 5248, 5510, 13, 5512, 11, 498, 646, 990, 279, 2860, 2473, 