{"id": "507", "question": "what are the characteristics of tropical rainforest floor", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor are:\n\n1. High levels of rainfall, with some areas receiving up to 400 inches of rain annually.\n2. High humidity due to the large amount of rainfall.\n3. Abundant vegetation, including tall trees, vines, ferns, herbs, mushrooms, fruits, and nuts.\n4. Quick decay of plant and animal matter due to the heat and moisture, which provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow.\n5. Presence of bananas growing on vines.\n\nTherefore, the tropical rainforest floor is characterized by high rainfall, humidity, and lush vegetation, with a diverse array of plant species and a rapid rate of decay and nutrient cycling.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the tropical rainforest floor has herbs and mushrooms growing on it. It also receives a large amount of rainfall, with some areas getting up to 400 inches annually, and the climate is very humid due to the constant warmth and moisture. The heat and moisture cause dead plants and animals to rot quickly, which releases rich nutrients into the soil, supporting the growth of other plants.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the tropical rainforest floor has herbs and mushrooms growing on it. It also receives a large amount of rainfall, with some areas getting up to 400 inches annually, and the climate is very humid due to the constant warmth and moisture. The heat and moisture cause dead plants and animals to rot quickly, which releases rich nutrients into the soil, supporting the growth of other plants.", "time_sec": 14.971, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 6422, 702, 41293, 323, 47151, 7826, 389, 432, 13, 1084, 1083, 21189, 264, 3460, 3311, 315, 52858, 11, 448, 1045, 5671, 3709, 705, 311, 220, 19, 15, 15, 14924, 29071, 11, 323, 279, 9977, 374, 1602, 65938, 4152, 311, 279, 6783, 40363, 323, 31157, 13, 576, 8628, 323, 31157, 5240, 5593, 10779, 323, 9898, 311, 5749, 6157, 11, 892, 19232, 9080, 36393, 1119, 279, 17171, 11, 12613, 279, 6513, 315, 1008, 10779, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0007, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0221, -0.1059, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.4285, -0.0509, -0.0016, -0.0, -0.0703, -0.0009, -0.0, -0.0345, -0.7906, -0.6583, -0.4578, -1.0177, -1.2654, -0.0093, -0.0, -0.3973, -0.6257, -0.2992, -0.8044, -0.0418, -0.0742, -0.3205, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0014, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.4532, -1.0108, -0.7607, -1.2245, -1.3212, -0.1111, -0.1622, -0.0435, -0.6169, -0.0, -0.9463, -1.138, -1.078, -0.0093, -0.1596, -0.0784, -0.4635, -0.5181, -0.0141, -0.1997, -0.0201, -0.1196, -0.0218, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0033, -0.2762, -0.0091, -0.0129, -1.0969, -0.421, -0.1233, -0.0001, -0.2825, -0.0, -0.012, -0.8391, -0.3938, -0.6512, -0.013, -0.0001, -0.813, -0.0626, -0.1331, -0.8691], "cumulative_logprob": -23.9625, "norm_logp": -0.2853, "input_len": 639, "output_tokens": 84, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.65, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "518", "question": "how do raffles work", "gt": "Raffles work by selling tickets to participants, who have the opportunity to win prizes. The specific details and mechanics of a raffle can vary. In a reverse raffle, participants purchase tickets with numbers on them, and the last ticket drawn wins the main prize. In a 50-50 draw, tickets are sold during an event, and 50% of the proceeds go to the winner of a random draw, while the other 50% is allocated for a charitable purpose. In some cases, raffles may also offer additional opportunities to win prizes, such as cash tip board raffles.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, raffles work by selling tickets to participants, with each ticket having a unique number. In a reverse raffle, tickets are drawn one by one, and the last remaining ticket wins. Tickets are sold at $50 each, and a table of 20 individuals collectively buys one $1000 ticket. There are also additional prizes like $500 early bird and first ticket pulled prizes. In a 50-50 draw, tickets are sold during an event, and 50% of the total sales go to the winner of a random draw, while the other 50% supports a charity. Some raffles, like cash tip board raffles, offer additional chances to win, such as $10,000, and are not included in the ticket price.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, raffles work by selling tickets to participants, with each ticket having a unique number. In a reverse raffle, tickets are drawn one by one, and the last remaining ticket wins. Tickets are sold at $50 each, and a table of 20 individuals collectively buys one $1000 ticket. There are also additional prizes like $500 early bird and first ticket pulled prizes. In a 50-50 draw, tickets are sold during an event, and 50% of the total sales go to the winner of a random draw, while the other 50% supports a charity. Some raffles, like cash tip board raffles, offer additional chances to win, such as $10,000, and are not included in the ticket price.", "time_sec": 28.985, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 435, 80535, 975, 553, 11236, 14403, 311, 13026, 11, 448, 1817, 11727, 3432, 264, 4911, 1372, 13, 758, 264, 9931, 435, 44090, 11, 14403, 525, 14764, 825, 553, 825, 11, 323, 279, 1537, 9664, 11727, 14816, 13, 35615, 525, 6088, 518, 400, 20, 15, 1817, 11, 323, 264, 1965, 315, 220, 17, 15, 7775, 44825, 49531, 825, 400, 16, 15, 15, 15, 11727, 13, 2619, 525, 1083, 5107, 37408, 1075, 400, 20, 15, 15, 4124, 11958, 323, 1156, 11727, 13238, 37408, 13, 758, 264, 220, 20, 15, 12, 20, 15, 4038, 11, 14403, 525, 6088, 2337, 458, 1538, 11, 323, 220, 20, 15, 4, 315, 279, 2790, 6625, 728, 311, 279, 13632, 315, 264, 4194, 4038, 11, 1393, 279, 1008, 220, 20, 15, 4, 11554, 264, 22846, 13, 4329, 435, 80535, 11, 1075, 8350, 11552, 4479, 435, 80535, 11, 3010, 5107, 16963, 311, 3164, 11, 1741, 438, 400, 16, 15, 11, 15, 15, 15, 11, 323, 525, 537, 5230, 304, 279, 11727, 3349, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0048, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0148, -0.0, -0.1198, -0.1566, -0.0119, -0.4896, -0.2062, -0.0176, -0.9262, -0.5563, -0.5243, -0.0013, -0.8861, -0.0106, -0.3004, -0.0424, -0.5934, -0.0615, -0.021, -0.0133, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0023, -0.4769, -0.2744, -0.8545, -0.1834, -0.2541, -0.0, -0.2454, -0.0242, -0.1815, -0.6347, -0.4016, -0.0153, -0.0844, -0.5185, -1.1368, -1.0071, -1.1147, -0.5504, -0.2691, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0028, -0.2241, -0.2571, -0.2613, -0.2707, -0.0638, -0.127, -0.0, 0.0, -0.2572, -1.1319, -1.2171, -0.1004, -0.5571, -0.0, -0.062, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0409, -0.7969, -1.1545, -0.1674, -0.2105, -1.2624, -0.6485, -0.8011, -1.1282, -0.0036, -0.0, -0.0, -0.8528, -0.0013, -0.2926, -0.0647, -0.3863, -0.1944, -0.9397, -0.0226, -0.1628, -0.0678, -0.0078, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0002, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0707, -0.0103, -0.6894, -0.0364, -0.0026, -0.183, -0.135, -0.0, -0.3769, -0.3349, -0.3488, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0485