{"id": "735", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "gt": "SMS stands for Short Message Service, commonly referred to as a text message, and allows you to send a text message of up to 160 characters to another device. MMS, which stands for Multimedia Messaging Service, is an evolution of SMS. It allows you to send messages that include pictures, video, or audio content to another device. MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB. SMS is restricted to sending text-only messages, whereas MMS allows a combination of text, pictures, sounds, and videos.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, SMS (Short Message Service) is a text-only messaging service that allows sending messages up to 160 characters, with longer messages split into parts. It is supported by most cell phones and is limited to text. MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is an evolution of SMS that allows sending multimedia content such as pictures, videos, audio, and text in combination. MMS messages can be larger in size, up to 300KB, and support formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF. While SMS is restricted to text, MMS supports richer content types.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, SMS (Short Message Service) is a text-only messaging service that allows sending messages up to 160 characters, with longer messages split into parts. It is supported by most cell phones and is limited to text. MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is an evolution of SMS that allows sending multimedia content such as pictures, videos, audio, and text in combination. MMS messages can be larger in size, up to 300KB, and support formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF. While SMS is restricted to text, MMS supports richer content types.", "time_sec": 24.423, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 29909, 320, 12472, 4856, 5362, 8, 374, 264, 1467, 15382, 295