{"id": "97", "question": "typical weather in indiana", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the typical weather in Indiana includes long, warm, humid, and wet summers, and chilly and windy winters. The temperature ranges from 22°F to 85°F throughout the year. The passages also mention snowfall and snow accumulation in specific cities, but do not provide a comprehensive overview of the typical weather in Indiana. Therefore, it is not possible to provide a complete answer based solely on the given passages.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, typical weather in Indiana features long, warm, humid, and wet summers, and chilly, windy winters. The temperature typically ranges from 22°F to 85°F throughout the year, rarely dropping below 3°F or rising above 92°F. The state experiences partly cloudy conditions year-round. Precipitation varies significantly, with the wettest year recorded in 1876 at Indianapolis (57.65 inches of rain) and the driest in 1934 (24.97 inches). Snowfall also varies, with the most recorded in one season being 74.5 inches in Rockford in 1979. Maximum monthly precipitation exceeded 16 inches in July 2003 and 2004 at Kokomo.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, typical weather in Indiana features long, warm, humid, and wet summers, and chilly, windy winters. The temperature typically ranges from 22°F to 85°F throughout the year, rarely dropping below 3°F or rising above 92°F. The state experiences partly cloudy conditions year-round. Precipitation varies significantly, with the wettest year recorded in 1876 at Indianapolis (57.65 inches of rain) and the driest in 1934 (24.97 inches). Snowfall also varies, with the most recorded in one season being 74.5 inches in Rockford in 1979. Maximum monthly precipitation exceeded 16 inches in July 2003 and 2004 at Kokomo.", "time_sec": 28.811, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389,