{"id": "104", "question": "how the body systems work together", "gt": "The body systems work together in order to maintain the normal functioning of the human body. These systems include the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, reproductive, and nervous systems. Each system has its own specific functions, but they also work in conjunction with one another to ensure the overall well-being of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from various systems such as the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. Similarly, the respiratory system provides oxygen to all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, body systems work together to maintain normal functioning. The urinary system cleans waste from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system supplies oxygen to all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. Both systems collaborate with others to ensure proper bodily function.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, body systems work together to maintain normal functioning. The urinary system cleans waste from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system supplies oxygen to all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. Both systems collaborate with others to ensure proper bodily function.", "time_sec": 13.571, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 311, 10306, 4622, 30201, 13, 576, 71635, 1849, 3