{"id": "109", "question": "what is the difference between the leeward and windward islands?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the Windward Islands are located in the southeastern part of the Caribbean Sea and are exposed to the wind (\"windward\") of the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies), while the Leeward Islands are located in the northwestern part of the Lesser Antilles and are away from the wind (\"lee\"). The main difference between them is their exposure to the wind and the resulting climate. The Windward Islands get more rain and are wetter due to their exposure to the wind, while the Leeward Islands are drier but still get rain.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the Windward Islands are exposed to the northeast trade winds and are wetter, receiving more rain, while the Leeward Islands are away from the wind and are drier. The Windward Islands are the southeastern islands of the Lesser Antilles, whereas the Leeward Islands are the northwestern islands. The Windward side of a mountain is closer to the ocean and gets more rain, while the Leeward side is farther from the shore and is drier.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the Windward Islands are exposed to the northeast trade winds and are wetter, receiving more rain, while the Leeward Islands are away from the wind and are drier. The Windward Islands are the southeastern islands of the Lesser Antilles, whereas the Leeward Islands are the northwestern islands. The Windward side of a mountain is closer to the ocean and gets more rain, while the Leeward side is farther from the shore and is drier.", "time_sec": 16.844, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 22087, 1606, 22235, 525, 14900, 311, 279, 40829, 6559, 28492, 323, 525, 14401, 465, 11, 12308, 803, 11174, 11, 1393, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 525, 3123, 504, 279, 9956, 323, 525, 294,