{"id": "300", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "gt": "To make a hot water heater circulate, one can install a recirculation system. The system consists of a pump that pulls hot water from the water heater and simultaneously sends cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused. This ensures that hot water is always available without having to wait for it to circulate naturally. Recirculation systems can be controlled by a button, timer, or motion sensor.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate, use a hot water circulation pump that sends cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater through a return line. This pump continuously circulates water through the water heater to keep it hot. Alternatively, demand systems can be used, which circulate hot water when activated by a push of a button, a timer, or a motion sensor.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate, use a hot water circulation pump that sends cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater through a return line. This pump continuously circulates water through the water heater to keep it hot. Alternatively, demand systems can be used, which circulate hot water when activated by a push of a button, a timer, or a motion sensor.", "time_sec": 14.918, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1281, 264, 4017, 3015, 42238, 4225, 6334, 11, 990, 264, 4017, 3015, 34755, 13834, 429, 21308, 7010, 3015, 504, 279, 4017, 3015, 5128, 1182, 311, 279, 3015, 42238, 1526, 264, 470, 1555, 13, 1096, 13834, 30878, 4225, 23156, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 311, 2506, 432, 4017, 13, 38478, 11, 7479, 5942, 646, 387, 1483, 11, 892, 4225, 6334, 4017, 3015, 979, 21985, 553, 264, 4484, 315, 264, 3137, 11, 264, 9021, 11, 476, 2