{"id": "609", "question": "how to do employee schedules", "gt": "To create employee schedules, start by making a list of all employees and the tasks they can perform. Then, create a chart with the work days and hours for each day. You can use scheduling software, a word processing program, or a sheet of paper to do this. Afterward, print out copies for employees or send schedules to their email accounts. It's also important to maintain a master schedule for making any necessary changes. Microsoft Excel can be used to create a work schedule for multiple employees, which can be modified as your business expands.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to do employee schedules, first make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform. Then, make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day. You can create the schedule using scheduling software, a word processing program, or a sheet of paper. After creating the schedule, print out copies for employees or send the schedules to their email accounts. Keep a master schedule to make any necessary changes. Microsoft Excel can be used to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing you to reuse the template as your business grows.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to do employee schedules, first make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform. Then, make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day. You can create the schedule using scheduling software, a word processing program, or a sheet of paper. After creating the schedule, print out copies for employees or send the schedules to their email accounts. Keep a master schedule to make any necessary changes. Microsoft Excel can be used to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing you to reuse the template as your business grows.", "time_sec": 20.069, "record_process": true, "token_ids"