{"id": "649", "question": "color of urin meaning", "gt": "The color of urine can indicate different health conditions. Red urine may indicate the presence of blood and could be a sign of an infection or cancer. Deep purple urine can be a characteristic of porphyria, a rare disorder. The normal color of urine is pale yellow due to the pigment urochrome.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the normal color of urine is pale yellow due to the pigment urochrome. However, urine color can change for various reasons. Seeing red urine typically indicates blood in the urine, which may signal serious conditions like infection or cancer. Deep purple urine is characteristic of porphyria, a rare inherited disorder. Additionally, certain foods like beets, berries, and fava beans, as well as some medications, can alter urine color. In kidney diseases, malfunctioning filtration and re-absorption processes can also change urine color from its normal pale yellow.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the normal color of urine is pale yellow due to the pigment urochrome. However, urine color can change for various reasons. Seeing red urine typically indicates blood in the urine, which may signal serious conditions like infection or cancer. Deep purple urine is characteristic of porphyria, a rare inherited disorder. Additionally, certain foods like beets, berries, and fava beans, as well as some medications, can alter urine color. In kidney diseases, malfunctioning filtration and re-absorption processes can also change urine color from its normal pale yellow.", "time_sec": 19.953, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 4622, 1894, 315, 39235, 374, 27539, 13753, 4152, 311, 279, 76578, 575, 299, 31902, 13, 4354, 11, 39235, 1894, 646, 2297, 369, 5257, 7966, 13, 55024, 2518, 39235, 11136, 14807, 6543, 304, 279, 39235, 11, 892, 1231,