{"id": "729", "question": "how do you process the air you breathe before it gets to your lungs?", "gt": "The process of air reaching the lungs involves the diaphragm muscle, which is the principal muscle of breathing. When the diaphragm contracts, it moves down from the bottom of the rib cage towards the abdominal region, allowing air to enter the lungs. This is part of the ventilation component of breathing, which is the movement of oxygen into, and carbon dioxide out of the lungs. Additionally, increasing the volume of the thoracic cavity pulls the lungs along with it, increasing their volume and causing a decrease in air pressure. This forces air from the atmosphere into the lungs, causing inhalation.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs. Before air reaches the lungs, the volume of the thoracic cavity increases, which drags the lungs along with it. This increase in lung volume causes a decrease in air pressure inside the lungs below atmospheric pressure, forcing air from the atmosphere into the lungs, resulting in inhalation. The diaphragm muscle plays a key role in this process by contracting and moving down from the bottom of the rib cage toward the abdominal region, thereby increasing the thoracic cavity volume.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs. Before air reaches the lungs, the volume of the thoracic cavity increases, which drags the lungs along with it. This increase in lung volume causes a decrease in air pressure inside the lungs below atmospheric pressure, forcing air from the atmosphere into the lungs, resulting in inhalation. The diaphragm muscle plays a key role in this process by contracting and moving down from the bottom of the rib cage toward the abdominal region, thereby increasing the thoracic cavity volume.", "time_sec": 23.654, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 1882, 315, 25938, 17601, 55134, 11, 892, 374, 279, 7203, 315, 23552, 1119, 323, 12499, 39489, 700, 315, 279, 44174, 13, 13235, 3720, 24491, 279, 44174, 11, 279, 8123, 315, 279, 72733, 93157, 55329, 12703, 11, 892, 1353, 2032, 279, 44174, 3156, 448, 432, 13, 1096, 5263, 304, 20622, 8123, 11137, 264, 18472, 304, 3720, 7262, 4766, 279, 44174, 3685, 44375, 7262, 11, 24913, 3720, 504, 279, 16566, 1119, 279, 44174, 11, 12942, 304, 76673, 367, 13, 576, 1853, 94796, 76, 15747, 11088, 264, 1376, 3476, 304, 419, 1882, 553, 59406, 323, 7218, 1495, 504, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 20131, 35360, 8841, 279, 55956, 5537, 11, 27492, 7703, 279, 72733, 93157, 55329, 8123, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0048, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.6697, -0.7535, -0.057, -0.5147, -0.3111, -0.6888, -0.0797, -0.0166, -0.0417, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.3139, -0.0002, -0.4524, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.3485, -0.0, -0.0231, -1.0508, -0.0773, -0.0593, -0.0381, -0.0004, -0.0009, -0.2188, -0.735, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0564, -0.0724, -0.2722, -0.4528, -0.0, -0.633, -0.0, -0.0722, -0.9142, -0.0002, -0.276, -0.0273, -0.6106, -0.0005, -0.2026, -0.0, -0.2288, -0.0625, -0.0115, -0.0, -0.0678, -0.0, -0.2536, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.4315, -0.1323, -0.0, -0.3871, -0.4296, -0.0152, -0.0167, -0.0002, -0.0813, -0.1015, -0.0, -0.0, -0.6369, -1.0692, -0.0, -0.0018, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.9374, -0.1077, 0.0, -0.0, -0.2586, -0.835, -0.0036, -0.1938, -0.0001, -0.7368, -0.0007, -0.0352, -0.1533, -0.0006, -0.0449, -0.0002, -0.5816, -0.0383, -0.0011, -0.129, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0, -0.0182, -0.4148, -0.0, -0.0015, -0.0298, -0.1889, -0.7232, -0.4218, -0.2834, -0.279, -0.0, -0.0552, -0.6653, -0.4108, -0.4147], "cumulative_logprob": -21.9417, "norm_logp": -0.1798, "input_len": 579, "output_tokens": 