{"id": "736", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "gt": "The difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS allows you to send text-only messages of up to 160 characters, while MMS allows you to send messages with pictures, sounds, videos, and text, with a larger content size of up to 300KB.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, SMS (Short Message Service) is a text-only messaging service that allows sending messages up to 160 characters, with longer messages split into parts. It is supported by most cell phones and is limited to text. MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is an evolution of SMS that allows sending multimedia content such as pictures, videos, audio, and text in combination. MMS messages can be larger in size, up to 300KB, and support formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF. While SMS is restricted to text, MMS supports richer content types.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, SMS (Short Message Service) is a text-only messaging service that allows sending messages up to 160 characters, with longer messages split into parts. It is supported by most cell phones and is limited to text. MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is an evolution of SMS that allows sending multimedia content such as pictures, videos, audio, and text in combination. MMS messages can be larger in size, up to 300KB, and support formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF. While SMS is restricted to text, MMS supports richer content types.", "time_sec": 24.937, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 29909, 320, 12472, 4856, 5362, 8, 374, 264, 1467, 15382, 29522, 2473, 429, 6147, 11628, 6605, 705, 311, 220, 16, 21, 15, 5766, 11, 448, 5021, 6605, 6718, 1119, 5479, 13, 1084, 374, 7248, 553, 1429, 2779, 17619, 323, 374, 7199, 311, 1467, 13, 386, 4826, 320, 40404, 26936, 73170, 5362, 8, 374, 458, 15379, 315, 29909, 429, 6147, 11628, 56513, 