{"id": "57", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "gt": "To prevent birds from building a nest on your porch, you can attach bird netting to the eves and top of your porch with staples. Additionally, you can install bird netting over your light fixture to deter birds from accessing it. Another option is to mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare the birds away. It's important to note that any product used to deter birds should be nonflammable and safe to use.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, you can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun. If your porch has open rafters, use the staple gun to attach the netting to the top of the porch. The netting prevents birds from accessing spaces where they often build nests. Additionally, you can install a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare birds away, but move it periodically so they do not become accustomed to it. These methods help prevent birds from nesting, which can block ventilation systems, use flammable materials, and spread disease through droppings.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, you can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun. If your porch has open rafters, use the staple gun to attach the netting to the top of the porch. The netting prevents birds from accessing spaces where they often build nests. Additionally, you can install a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare birds away, but move it periodically so they do not become accustomed to it. These methods help prevent birds from nesting, which can block ventilation systems, use flammable materials, and spread disease through droppings.", "time_sec": 23.116, "record_process": true, "