{"id": "86", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "gt": "To prepare a blood slide, you will need a clean glass slide and a drop of blood. Place the slide on a flat surface and add a small drop of blood to one end of the slide. Take another clean slide and touch the blood with one end at a 45-degree angle so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to create a thin smear of blood. Make two smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly before placing them in slide transport containers.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to prepare a blood slide follow these steps: STEP ONE: Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface and add one small drop of blood to one end. STEP TWO: Take another clean slide, hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees, touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge by capillary action, then carefully push it along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear. STEP THREE: Make two smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly. Once dried, place the slides in provided slide transport containers.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to prepare a blood slide follow these steps: STEP ONE: Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface and add one small drop of blood to one end. STEP TWO: Take another clean slide, hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees, touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge by capillary action, then carefully push it along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear. STEP THREE: Make two smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly. Once dried, place the slides in provided slide transport containers.", "time_sec": 21.817, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 10549, 264, 6543, 14983, 1795, 1493, 7354, 25, 48356,