{"id": "111", "question": "what is the difference between the leeward and windward islands?", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the main difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is their exposure to the wind and precipitation. The Windward Islands are exposed to the northeasterly trade winds and receive more rainfall, making them wetter and more humid, while the Leeward Islands are located on the leeward side of the mountains and receive less rainfall, making them drier. Therefore, the answer to the question is:\n\nThe Windward Islands are wetter and more humid due to their exposure to the northeasterly trade winds, while the Leeward Islands are drier and receive less rainfall.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the Windward Islands are exposed to the northeast trade winds and are wetter, receiving more rain, while the Leeward Islands are away from the wind and are drier. The Windward Islands are the southeastern islands of the Lesser Antilles, whereas the Leeward Islands are the northwestern islands. The Windward side of a mountain is closer to the ocean and gets more rain, while the Leeward side is farther from the shore and is drier.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the Windward Islands are exposed to the northeast trade winds and are wetter, receiving more rain, while the Leeward Islands are away from the wind and are drier. The Windward Islands are the southeastern islands of the Lesser Antilles, whereas the Leeward Islands are the northwestern islands. The Windward side of a mountain is closer to the ocean and gets more rain, while the Leeward side is farther from the shore and is drier.", "time_sec": 16.898, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 22087, 1606, 22235, 525, 14900, 311, 279, 40829, 6559, 28492, 323, 525, 14401, 465, 11, 12308, 803, 11174, 11, 1393, 279, 1967, 24035, 