{"id": "129", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "gt": "What are the dimensions of the shed in passage 3?\n\nThe dimensions of the shed in passage 3 are 6 feet long by 4 feet wide.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Cut two 4x4 skids to 70 2/4 inches and set them level. Cut two 2x6 rim joists to 7 3/4 inches and six joists to 44 3/4 inches, then assemble the floor frame and set it on the skids. Check for square and anchor the frame using four joist clip angles. Alternatively, cut two pressure-treated 4x4s to 6 feet for skids, position the frame, toenail floor joists to skids, and attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring. Walls are built separately and raised onto the frame. The shed dimensions can be 6 feet by 4 feet or expanded in 2 or 4-foot increments.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Cut two 4x4 skids to 70 2/4 inches and set them level. Cut two 2x6 rim joists to 7 3/4 inches and six joists to 44 3/4 inches, then assemble the floor frame and set it on the skids. Check for square and anchor the frame using four joist clip angles. Alternatively, cut two pressure-treated 4x4s to 6 feet for skids, position the frame, toenail floor joists to skids, and attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring. Walls are built separately and raised onto the frame. The shed dimensions can be 6 feet by 4 feet or expanded in 2 or 4-foot increments.", "time_sec": 31.824, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 4752, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 17601, 3807, 7354, 13, 5512, 11, 10549, 279, 2747, 448, 264, 220, 19, 24241, 6193, 315, 16830, 291, 41523, 13, 19649, 1378, 220, 19, 87, 19, 1901, 