{"id": "158", "question": "how to factory reset a htc one vx", "gt": "To factory reset an HTC One VX, you can follow the steps mentioned in passage 3. Slide the Notifications panel open, tap on Storage, then Factory data reset, and finally tap on Reset phone and Erase everything.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to factory reset an HTC One VX, first ensure you back up any data and files you want to keep. Then, slide the Notifications panel open and tap on it. Next, tap on Storage, followed by Factory data reset. Tap on Reset phone and then tap Erase everything.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to factory reset an HTC One VX, first ensure you back up any data and files you want to keep. Then, slide the Notifications panel open and tap on it. Next, tap on Storage, followed by Factory data reset. Tap on Reset phone and then tap Erase everything.", "time_sec": 11.609, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 8633, 7585, 458, 48267, 3776, 78177, 11, 1156, 5978, 498, 1182, 705, 894, 821, 323, 3542, 498, 1366, 311, 2506, 13, 5005, 11, 14983, 279, 52938, 6945, 1787, 323, 15239, 389, 432, 13, 9295, 11, 15239, 389, 14693, 11, 8110, 553, 16937, 821, 7585, 13, 36134, 389, 16932, 4540, 323, 1221, 15239, 9740, 519, 4297, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0146, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0721, -0.0035, -0.0, -0.1931, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0589, -0.5006, -0.2522, -0.5419, -0.1184, 0.0, -0.0318, -0.6294, -0.0773, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.0383, -0.0, -0.0012, -0.0311, -0.0621, -0.084, -0.0594, -0.0011, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.1292, -0.0006, -0.1397, -0.4169, -0.0246, -0.275, -0.0, -0.0337, -0.3682, -0.0387, -0.591, -0.5835, -0.0, -0.0079, -0.0031, -0.0, -0.0027, -0.6372, -0.3499, -0.0037, -0.0, -0.576, -0.0763, -0.0709, -0.3137, -0.0, -0.0, -0.2257, -0.4246], "cumulative_logprob": -8.0649, "norm_logp": -0.126, "input_le