{"id": "236", "question": "average weather sausalito", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the average weather in Sausalito can be summarized as follows:\n\n* Temperature: The average temperature in Sausalito ranges from 50°F (December) to 58°F (September).\n* Precipitation: Sausalito receives an average of 34 inches of rain per year, with the most precipitation occurring in January (0 inches).\n* Air Quality Index: The air quality index in Sausalito is 13% better than the national average, but the pollution index is 61% worse than the national average.\n* Sunshine: Sausalito experiences 256 sunny days per year, with an average of 56 days with measurable precipitation.\n* Comfort Index: According to Sperling's comfort index, Sausalito has a score of 84 out of 100, indicating a comfortable year-round climate.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages regarding the average weather in Sausalito during a specific month or time period.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, Sausalito has an average yearly precipitation of 34 inches, with 56 days of measurable precipitation annually. The city receives 256 sunny days per year. The average temperature in July is around 69 degrees, while the January low is 43 degrees. The highest monthly average temperature occurs in September at 58 degrees, and the lowest monthly average temperature is in December at 50 degrees. Sausalito has no snowfall, with an average of 0 inches annually. The air quality index is 13% better than the national average, but the pollution index is 61% worse. Sausalito's comfort index is 84 out of 100, significantly higher than the US average of 54, indicating a more comfortable climate year-round.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, Sausalito has an average yearly precipitation of 34 inches, with 56 days of measurable precipitation annually. The city receives 256 sunny days per year. The average temperature in July is around 69 degrees, while the January low is 43 degrees. The highest monthly average temperature occurs in September at 58 degrees, and the lowest monthly average temperature is in December at 50 degrees. Sausalito has no snowfall, with an average of 0 inches annually. The air quality index is 13% better than the national average, but the pollution index is 61% worse. Sausalito's comfort index is 84 out of 100, significantly higher than the US average of 54, indicating a more comfortable climate year-round.", "time_sec": 28.678, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 328, 79074, 6357, 702, 458, 5461, 44270, 59950, 315, 220, 18, 19, 14924, 11, 448, 220, 20, 21, 2849, 315, 65203, 59950, 29071, 13, 576, 3283, 21189, 220, 17, 20, 21, 39698, 2849, 817, 1042, 13, 576, 5461, 9315, 304, 5768, 374, 2163, 220, 21, 24, 12348, 11, 1393, 279, 6058, 3347, 374, 220, 19, 18, 12348, 13, 576, 8426, 15088, 5461, 9315, 13666, 304, 6122, 518, 220, 20, 23, 12348, 11, 323, 279, 15457, 15088, 5461, 9315, 374, 304, 6652, 518, 220, 20, 15, 12348, 13, 328, 79074, 6357, 702, 902, 11794, 13464, 11, 448, 458, 5461, 315, 220, 15, 14924, 29071, 13, 576, 3720, 4271, 1922, 374, 220, 16, 18, 4, 2664, 1091, 279, 5313, 5461, 11, 714, 279, 24761, 1922, 374, 220, 21, 16, 4, 10960, 13, 328, 79074, 6357, 594, 6838, 1922, 374, 220, 23, 19, 700, 315, 220, 16, 15, 15, 11, 11941, 5080, 1091, 279, 2274, 5461, 315, 220, 20, 19, 11, 18860, 264, 803, 10655, 9977, 1042, 21015, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0004, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.3578, -0.0, -0.0, -0.1515, -0.2848, -0.1003, -0.3983, -0.6387, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0, -0.2051, -0.4067, -0.8701, -0.2105, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.1828, -0.006, -0.3344, -0.5344, -0.2086, -0.7245, -0.3172, -0.6969, -0.1658, -0.1609, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.2016, -0.0, -0.9261, -0.6673, -0.5847, -1.1331, -0.1135, -0.0467, -0.1092, -0.1371, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.2017, -0.6376, -0.5194, -0.6396