{"id": "245", "question": "difference between feha and ada", "gt": "One difference between FEHA and ADA is that the ADA applies to all private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while FEHA affects more employees and doesn't distinguish between private and public employers like ADA does.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, one difference between FEHA and ADA is that the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while FEHA covers more employees and applies to both private and public employers without such distinctions. Another key difference is in the definition of disability: under the ADA, a physical or mental impairment must substantially limit a major life activity, whereas under FEHA, it only needs to limit a major life activity, not necessarily substantially.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, one difference between FEHA and ADA is that the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while FEHA covers more employees and applies to both private and public employers without such distinctions. Another key difference is in the definition of disability: under the ADA, a physical or mental impairment must substantially limit a major life activity, whereas under FEHA, it only needs to limit a major life activity, not necessarily substantially.", "time_sec": 16.078, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 825, 6672, 1948, 27931, 17020, 323, 78325, 374, 429, 279, 78325, 16790, 311, 869, 10486, 22426, 448, 3040, 311, 36655, 8256, 11, 1393, 27931, 17020, 14521, 803, 8256, 323, 16790, 311, 2176, 869, 323, 584, 22426, 2041, 1741, 86159, 13, 13293, 1376, 6672, 374, 304, 279, 7271, 315, 27254, 25, 1212, 279, 78325, 11, 264, 6961, 476, 10502, 52217, 1969, 31202, 3930, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 11, 19853, 1212, 27931, 17020, 11, 432, 1172, 3880, 311, 3930,