{"id": "401", "question": "2006 chevy remove door panel", "gt": "To remove the door panel on a 2006 Chevy, first remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup and one in the middle of the inside door handle. Additionally, there's a pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place which needs to be removed. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off. Ensure to remove all screws and clips in the door panel and gently pull the panel away from the frame. Finally, remove any wiring connections and the panel will come off the frame.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup and one screw in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door, there is a pin that holds the panel in place and must be removed. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the panel off the rear door. If needed, use a screwdriver to remove all screws and clips, gently pull the panel away from the frame, and disconnect any wiring connections before removing the panel completely. An instructional video is also available to guide the process.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup and one screw in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door, there is a pin that holds the panel in place and must be removed. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the panel off the rear door. If needed, use a screwdriver to remove all screws and clips, gently pull the panel away from the frame, and disconnect any wiring connections before removing the panel completely. An instructional video is also available to guide the process.", "time_sec": 23.034, "record_process": true, "