{"id": "530", "question": "how does ez pass charges work", "gt": "Sure! Based on the given passages, here is how E-ZPass charging works:\n\nWhen you sign up for E-ZPass, a certain amount is charged to your credit card to establish a balance (specifically, $100 for the EZ-Tag and $25 for the TX-Tag). This balance is used to pay for tolls as you drive through toll lanes. When you drive through a toll booth, the toll tag mounted on your windshield is read by the antennae, and your E-ZPass account is charged the appropriate amount. The amount is deducted from your balance. If your balance falls below a certain threshold ($10 for the TX-Tag), E-ZPass will charge your credit card an additional $100 or $25 to top up your balance.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, E-ZPass charges work by reading the toll tag mounted on your vehicle's windshield as it enters the toll lane. The system uses antennae to detect the tag and automatically charges your E-ZPass account the proper toll amount as your vehicle passes through. If your vehicle does not have a toll tag, the system classifies you as a violator and takes photos of your license plate for processing.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, E-ZPass charges work by reading the toll tag mounted on your vehicle's windshield as it enters the toll lane. The system uses antennae to detect the tag and automatically charges your E-ZPass account the proper toll amount as your vehicle passes through. If your vehicle does not have a toll tag, the system classifies you as a violator and takes photos of your license plate for processing.", "time_sec": 15.119, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 468, 11171, 12187, 10195, 975, 553, 5290, 279, 25851, 4772, 21810, 389, 697, 7310, 594, 73939, 438, 432, 28833, 279, 25851, 21272, 13, 576, 1849, 5711, 71477, 5918, 311, 11140, 279, 4772, 323,