{"id": "541", "question": "lyrics he was a friend of mine", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the lyrics \"he was a friend of mine\" are from the song \"He Was a Friend of Mine\" written by Bob Dylan.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the lyrics \"he was a friend of mine\" are repeated multiple times in the song. Specific lines include: \"He was a friend of mine he was a friend of mine. He died without a penny he didn't have a dime he was a friend of mine. He died neath the midnight sun he died neath the midnight sun.\" Additional lyrics from the song include: \"And I never been quite satisfied. And he was a friend of mine. He never done no wrong. He never done no wrong. A thousand miles from home. And he never harmed no one. And he was a friend of mine. He was a friend of mine. He was a friend of mine. Every time I hear his name. Lord, I just can't keep from cryin'. 'Cause he was a friend of mine.\" The song is credited to songwriter Bob Dylan.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the lyrics \"he was a friend of mine\" are repeated multiple times in the song. Specific lines include: \"He was a friend of mine he was a friend of mine. He died without a penny he didn't have a dime he was a friend of mine. He died neath the midnight sun he died neath the midnight sun.\" Additional lyrics from the song include: \"And I never been quite satisfied. And he was a friend of mine. He never done no wrong. He never done no wrong. A thousand miles from home. And he never harmed no one. And he was a friend of mine. He was a friend of mine. He was a friend of mine. Every time I hear his name. Lord, I just can't keep from cryin'. 'Cause he was a friend of mine.\" The song is credited to songwriter Bob Dylan.", "time_sec": 30.6, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 23261, 330, 383, 572, 264, 4238, 315, 10485, 1, 525, 