{"id": "601", "question": "which is better exercise cycling or aerobic", "gt": "The passages suggest that both cycling and aerobic exercise are beneficial. However, cycling, including stationary cycling, may be particularly ideal for individuals with arthritic or other orthopedic problems who may have difficulty walking for extended periods. Furthermore, stationary biking provides a low impact workout as it supports the majority of your weight. Therefore, while both exercises are valuable, the passages may imply that cycling could be better for those with specific physical conditions.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, cycling is a type of aerobic exercise that offers specific benefits. It is particularly suitable for individuals with arthritic or orthopedic issues who may find walking painful. The indoor stationary bike provides the lowest impact workout compared to equipment like treadmills and rowing machines because it supports most of the user's weight. While aerobic exercise like running is generally beneficial, cycling can be a better option for those with joint problems due to its low-impact nature.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, cycling is a type of aerobic exercise that offers specific benefits. It is particularly suitable for individuals with arthritic or orthopedic issues who may find walking painful. The indoor stationary bike provides the lowest impact workout compared to equipment like treadmills and rowing machines because it supports most of the user's weight. While aerobic exercise like running is generally beneficial, cycling can be a better option for those with joint problems due to its low-impact nature.", "time_sec": 17.119, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 32062, 374, 264, 943, 315, 90390, 10158, 429, 6081, 3151, 7567, 13, 1084, 374, 7945, 14452, 369, 7775, 448, 796, 339, 49208, 476, 29199, 16367, 292, 4714, 879, 1231, 1477, 11435, 25118, 13, 576, 29519, 52635, 12963, 5707, 279, 15457, 5421, 25242, 7707, 311, 7096, 1075, 47714, 76, 3305, 323, 2802, 287, 12645, 1576, 432, 11554, 1429, 315, 279, 1196, 594, 4680, 13, 5976, 90390, 10158, 1075, 4303, 374, 8789, 23699, 11, 32062, 646, 387, 264, 2664, 2999, 369, 1846, 448, 10284, 5322, 4152, 311, 1181, 3347, 12, 57300, 6993, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0004, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0009, -0.0, -0.0034, -0.2365, -0.0092, -0.0543, -0.5828, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.8354, -0.3304, -1.1652, -0.3871, -0.819, -0.9429, -0.2005, -0.2496, -0.6115, -0.0, -0.1856, -0.0797, -0.4306, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0086, -0.0, 0.0, -0.2713, -0.218, -0.1411, -0.6281, -0.0026, -0.2422, -0.189, -0.9745, -0.475, -0.2242, -0.0022, -0.1485, -0.2525, -0.0002, -0.0142, -0.0001, -0.5787, -0.0, -1.1036, -0.0298, -0.4445, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0621, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.7634, -0.0011, -0.0, -0.0309, -0.0001, -0.2826, -0.2344, -0.2014, -0.3869, -0.0637, -1.0668, -0.5536, -0.3367, -0.8435, -0.0013, -0.163, -0.3966, -0.6955, -0.1653, -0.0088, -1.4882, -0.0347, -0.0902, -0.2521, -0.7153, -0.043, -0.36, -0.5258, -0.885, -0.7298, -0.9443, -0.0, -0.0106, -0.8219, -0.0234, -0.0, -0.0016, -0.0805, -0.6681], "cumulative_logprob": -27.0062, "norm_logp": -0.2756, "input_len": 437, "output_tokens": 98, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.4, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "610", "question": "how to do employee schedules", "gt": "To create an employee schedule, start by making a list of all employees and their duties (Passage 2). Then, create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day (Passage 2). Print out copies of the schedule for employees or send them via email (Passage 3). If you need to make any changes, keep a master schedule and update it as needed (Passage 3). Microsoft Excel is a useful tool for creating schedules for multiple employees and can be used as your business grows (Passage 3). It's important to note that there may be other work laws that you need to follow, such as paying overtime if you schedule an employee more than 40 hours per week (Passage 1).", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to do employee schedules, first make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform. Then, make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day. You can create the schedule using scheduling software, a word processing program, or a sheet of paper. After creating the schedule, print out copies for employees or send the schedules to their email accounts. Keep a master schedule to make any necessary changes. Microsoft Excel can be used to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing you to reuse the template as your business grows.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to do employee schedules, first make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform. Then, make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day. You can create the schedule using scheduling software, a word processing program, or a sheet of paper. After creating the schedule, print out copies for employees or send the schedules to their email accounts. Keep a master schedule to make any necessary changes. Microsoft Excel can be used to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing you to reuse the template as your business grows.", "time_sec": 20.07, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 653, 9364, 36769, 11, 1156, 1281, 264, 1140, 315, 678, 697, 8256, 323, 279, 21300, 807, 646, 2736, 13, 5005, 11, 1281, 264, 9487, 315, 279, 975, 2849, 323, 279, 4115, 369, 1817, 1899, 13, 1446, 646, 1855, 279, 9700, 1667, 37852, 3162, 11, 264, 3409, 8692, 2025, 11, 476, 264, 10834, 315, 5567, 13, 4636, 6825, 279, 9700, 11, 1173, 700, 10993, 369, 8256, 476, 3624, 279, 36769, 311, 862, 2551, 9618, 13, 13655, 264, 7341, 9700, 311, 1281, 894, 5871, 4344, 13, 5100, 21029, 646, 387, 1483, 311, 1855, 264, 975, 9700, 369, 5248, 8256, 11, 10693, 498, 311, 25978, 279, 3811, 438, 697, 2562, 27715, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0003, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0308, -0.1395, -0.0, -0.0, -0.7926, -0.2655, -0.0063, -0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0, -0.3869, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0031, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.025, -0.3146, -0.6099, -0.5759, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0012, -0.0, -0.0086, -0.0047, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0, -0.01, -0.0051, -0.0, -0.4746, -0.1954, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.314, -0.0002, 0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.2, -0.013, 0.0, 0.0, -0.006, -0.9473, -0.4481, -0.0079, -0.0006, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.3887, -0.0, -0.0011, -0.0021, -0.0, -0.0012, -0.9331, -0.5761, -0.1275, -0.0838, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0012, -0.0779, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.039, -0.2518, -0.2334, -0.0526, -0.3494, -0.0007, -0.2802, -0.1277, -0.0, -0.3143, -0.0052, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0046, -0.0432, -0.033, -0.0, -0.0149, -0.0, -0.0, -0.2659, -0.0712, -0.2014, -0.0, -0.1888, -0.0009, -0.3879, -0.0007, -0.0047, -0.0, -0.1272, -0.0003, -0.0078], "cumulative_logprob": -10.9897, "norm_logp": -0.0939, "input_len": 463, "output_tokens": 117, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 57.14, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "619", "question": "how to force removal of a printer in devices and printers", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the information provided in the passages, here are the steps to force remove a printer in Devices and Printers:\n\n1. Open Print Manager or Printers folder.\n2. Right-click the printer you want to remove and select Delete. If you can't delete the printer, run the command with administrative privileges by right-clicking the printer again and selecting \"Run as administrator\" before deleting it.\n3. Alternatively, you can remove the printer from the devices list, uninstall the Windows print drivers, and disconnect the printer from the computer if it's connected via USB. Restart the Spooler Service after removing the printer or printer port.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, first go to Control Panel, then click on Hardware and Sound, followed by clicking Printers. Right-click the printer you want to remove and click Delete. If you cannot delete the printer, right-click it again, select Run as administrator, and then click Delete.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, first go to Control Panel, then click on Hardware and Sound, followed by clicking Printers. Right-click the printer you want to remove and click Delete. If you cannot delete the printer, right-click it again, select Run as administrator, and then click Delete.", "time_sec": 12.679, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5344, 16652, 315, 264, 22380, 304, 40377, 323, 8213, 388, 11, 1156, 728, 311, 7779, 18946, 11, 1221, 4205, 389, 36765, 323, 14594, 11, 8110, 553, 18458, 8213, 388, 13, 10083, 28118, 279, 22380, 498, 1366, 311, 4057, 323,