{"id": "737", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "gt": "Based on the given passages, SMS stands for Short Message Service and allows you to send a message of up to 160 characters to another device. In contrast, MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows you to send a message including pictures, videos, sounds, text, or any combination of the four. The content of an MMS message has a maximum size of 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, GIF, etc.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, SMS (Short Message Service) is a text-only messaging service that allows sending messages up to 160 characters, with longer messages split into parts. It is supported by most cell phones and is limited to text. MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is an evolution of SMS that allows sending multimedia content such as pictures, videos, audio, and text in combination. MMS messages can be larger in size, up to 300KB, and support formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF. While SMS is restricted to text, MMS supports richer content types.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, SMS (Short Message Service) is a text-only messaging service that allows sending messages up to 160 characters, with longer messages split into parts. It is supported by most cell phones and is limited to text. MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is an evolution of SMS that allows sending multimedia content such as pictures, videos, audio, and text in combination. MMS messages can be larger in size, up to 300KB, and support formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF. While SMS is restricted to text, MMS supports richer content types.", "time_sec": 24.058, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 29909, 320, 12472, 4856, 5362, 8, 374, 264, 1467, 15382, 29522, 2473, 429, 6147, 11628, 6605, 705, 311, 220, 16, 21, 15, 5766, 11, 448, 5021, 6605, 6718, 1119, 5479, 13, 1084, 374, 7248