{"id": "130", "question": "difference between vietnam and india", "gt": "The passages suggest that trends in India are more typical than those in Vietnam, particularly in the area of education. Vietnam's education system is described as relatively equitable, where poorer children receive the same treatment as their better-off counterparts. In contrast, India's early focus was on getting children into school, which involved setting up schools, and training teachers. Politically, India supported Vietnam's independence from France and opposed American involvement in the Vietnam War. Both countries have a history of colonialism, with India being a former colony of the United Kingdom and Vietnam of France. Post-colonization, India experienced division and conflict among Hindus, Muslims and Sikhs. Cultural and economic links between India and Vietnam date back to the 2nd century.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the education system in Vietnam is relatively equitable, meaning poorer children receive the same opportunities as wealthier children, while India's trends in education are described as much more typical, implying less equity. India's early focus was on getting children into school by establishing resources and facilities, whereas Vietnam's system ensures equal access. Politically, India supported Vietnam's independence from France and opposed American involvement in the Vietnam War, showing diplomatic alignment. Culturally, India and Vietnam have historical ties dating back to the 2nd century, with the Indic Chăm Pa kingdom influencing Vietnamese music. In terms of colonial history, the United Kingdom lost India in 1947, and France lost Indochina (modern-day Vietnam) in 1945, both colonies being economically significant to their colonizers. After decolonization, India experienced religious division among Hindus, Muslims, and Sikhs, leading to conflicts, while Vietnam's post-colonial situation is not detailed in the passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the education system in Vietnam is relatively equitable, meaning poorer children receive the same opportunities as wealthier children, while India's trends in education are described as much more typical, implying less equity. India's early focus was on getting children into school by establishing resources and facilities, whereas Vietnam's system ensures equal access. Politically, India supported Vietnam's independence from France and opposed American involvement in the Vietnam War, showing diplomatic alignment. Culturally, India and Vietnam have historical ties dating back to the 2nd century, with the Indic Chăm Pa kingdom influencing Vietnamese music. In terms of colonial history, the United Kingdom lost India in 1947, and France lost Indochina (modern-day Vietnam) in 1945, both colonies being economically significant to their colonizers. After decolonization, India experienced religious division among Hindus, Muslims, and Sikhs, leading to conflicts, while Vietnam's post-colonial situation is not detailed in the passages.", "time_sec": 34.777, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6731, 1849, 304, 22500, 374, 12040, 76009, 11, 7290, 65181, 2841, 5258, 279, 1852, 10488, 438, 11939, 1268, 2841, 11, 1393, 6747, 594, 18339, 304, 6731, 525, 7481, 438, 1753, 803, 14260, 11, 72867, 2686, 24448, 13, 6747, 594, 4124, 5244, 572, 389, 3709, 2841, 1119, 2906, 553, 30592, 4963, 323, 12786, 11, 19853, 22500, 594, 1849, 25351, 6144, 2615, 13, 15928, 2673, 11, 6747, 7248, 22500, 594, 23665, 504, 9625, 323, 16087, 3693, 21587, 304, 279, 22500, 5004, 11, 9027, 33516, 17189, 13, 25594, 41924, 11, 6747, 323, 22500, 614, 13656, 19818, 4924, 1182, 311, 279, 220, 17, 303, 9294, 11, 448, 279, 2263, 292, 910, 77354, 15681, 25079, 65600, 48477, 4627, 13, 758, 3793, 315, 36583, 3840, 11, 279, 3639, 15072, 5558, 6747, 304, 220,