{"id": "180", "question": "psychological effects of hugging", "gt": "Hugging has significant psychological effects. It creates a warm feeling that affects the entire body, akin to the effect of many drugs operating simultaneously. This could be due to the feeling of a loving embrace, leading to good relationships and emotional intimacy. It also enhances empathy and listening skills, which can lead to a psychological hug. Furthermore, research has found that hugging can significantly reduce worries about mortality and boost self-esteem. This soothing effect can be achieved even when hugging an inanimate object like a teddy bear.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, psychological effects of hugging include reducing worry of mortality as shown in a study published in Psychological Science, where hugging—even with an inanimate object like a teddy bear—soothes existential fears. Additionally, empathic listening skills can create a \"psychological hug,\" making individuals feel emotionally supported and fostering emotional intimacy, good relationships, and happy marriages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, psychological effects of hugging include reducing worry of mortality as shown in a study published in Psychological Science, where hugging—even with an inanimate object like a teddy bear—soothes existential fears. Additionally, empathic listening skills can create a \"psychological hug,\" making individuals feel emotionally supported and fostering emotional intimacy, good relationships, and happy marriages.", "time_sec": 13.976, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 23187, 6239, 315, 305, 35268, 2924, 17719, 10955, 315, 28428, 438, 6839, 304, 264, 3920, 4652, 304, 68969, 9965, 11, 1380, 305, 35268, 78978, 448, 458, 304, 22030, 1633, 1075, 264, 41223, 10258, 11722, 2293, 704, 78, 6375, 66639, 23209, 13, 22406, 11,