{"id": "189", "question": "how long does it take to make chicken tender in crock pot", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the answer to the question \"How long does it take to make chicken tender in a crock pot?\" is:\n\n6-8 hours on low heat, or 4 hours on high heat if you're short on time.\n\nThe first passage suggests cooking the chicken on low for 6-8 hours, or 1 hour on high and then 5 hours on low. The second passage repeats the same information. The third passage provides additional information that chicken breast will always come out tender as long as there is enough moisture, and suggests cooking it for 4 hours on high if you're short on time.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question is 6-8 hours on low heat, or 4 hours on high heat if you're short on time.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, chicken can be made tender in a crock pot by cooking it on low for 6 - 8 hours or on high for 1 hour followed by low for about 5 hours. Alternatively, chicken breasts can be cooked for 4 hours on high if time is limited, and it will still turn out tender as long as there is enough moisture.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, chicken can be made tender in a crock pot by cooking it on low for 6 - 8 hours or on high for 1 hour followed by low for about 5 hours. Alternatively, chicken breasts can be cooked for 4 hours on high if time is limited, and it will still turn out tender as long as there is enough moisture.", "time_sec": 13.946, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 16158, 646, 387, 1865, 27582, 304, 264, 14093, 377, 3338, 553, 17233, 432, 389, 3347, 369, 220, 21, 481, 220, 23, 4115, 476, 389, 1550, 369, 220, 16, 6460, 8110, 553, 3347, 369, 911, 220, 20, 4115, 13, 38478, 11, 16158, 36349, 646, 387, 29105, 369, 220, 19, 4115, 389, 1550, 421, 882, 374, 7199, 11, 323, 432, 686, 2058, 2484, 700, 27582, 438, 1293, 438, 1052, 374, 3322, 31157, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.5038, -0.1643, -0.0008, -0.576, -0.0002, -0.0028, -0.0002, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.0186, -0.0005, -0.0002, -0.4324, -0.01, -0.0, -0.0022, -0.0001, -0.0052, -0.8482, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.372, -0.5255, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0016, -0.0009, -0.0, -0.0036, -0.0, -0.0043, -0.0022, -0.0201, 0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0062, -0.941, -0.0001, -1.0285, -0.0489, -0.0117, -0.1649, -0.0001, -0.3137, -0.0015, -0.5231, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0329, -0.4869, -0.0, -0.0058, -0.4024, -0.1131, -0.7866, -0.0063, -0.0001, -0.0148, -0.0, -0.4744, -0.4408, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0036, -0.0002, -0.1028, -0.0, -0.0315, -0.1283], "cumulative_logprob": -9.567, "norm_logp": -0.1227, "input_len": 700, "output_tokens": 78, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 44.26, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "197", "question": "leasing meaning", "gt": "Leasing refers to a process in which a firm obtains the use of fixed assets by making contractual, periodic, and tax-deductible payments to the owner of those assets. The lessee is the party receiving the services or assets under the lease contract, while the lessor is the owner of the assets.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, leasing is a contractual arrangement where a firm or individual, known as the lessee, obtains the use of a fixed asset from another party, the lessor, in exchange for a series of periodic, tax-deductible payments. The lessor retains legal ownership of the asset while the lessee gains the right to use it. Common leased assets include property, buildings, vehicles, and industrial or business equipment. The agreement is governed by specific terms, and the payment made by the lessee is referred to as rent.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, leasing is a contractual arrangement where a firm or individual, known as the lessee, obtains the use of a fixed asset from another party, the lessor, in exchange for a series of periodic, tax-deductible payments. The lessor retains legal ownership of the asset while the lessee gains the right to use it. Common leased assets include property, buildings, vehicles, and industrial or business equipment. The agreement is governed by specific terms, and the payment made by the lessee is referred to as rent.", "time_sec": 19.433, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 70319, 374, 264, 75443, 26112, 1380, 264, 7474, 476, 3842, 11, 3881, 438, 279, 3541, 4060, 11, 93563, 279, 990, 315, 264, 8356, 9329, 504, 2441, 4614, 11, 279, 2686, 269, 11, 304, 9289, 369, 264, 4013, 315, 38345, 11, 3742, 1737, 80500, 1238, 14173, 13, 576, 2686, 269, 51844, 5777, 15278, 315, 279, 9329, 1393, 279, 3541, 4060, 19619, 279, 1290,