{"id": "227", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Here's a brief answer on how to fix a lift valve in a toilet based on the given passages:\n\nTo fix a lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\n\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n3. Install a new flapper valve and chain for a 1.6 gallon per flush toilet.\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n5. Adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links if necessary. Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\n6. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included, screw it in tightly.\n7. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened.\n8. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and take out any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm. Install the new flapper valve and connect the lift chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is closest to the edge. Use pliers to secure the connection. Push the solid end of the lift arm into the flush handle and tighten with a screw if included. Turn the water valve back on and flush the toilet to test. If the flush is slow, adjust the chain to be tighter. If needed, readjust the chain by moving the metal clip up or down a few links and cut off excess chain to prevent tangling.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and take out any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm. Install the new flapper valve and connect the lift chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is closest to the edge. Use pliers to secure the connection. Push the solid end of the lift arm into the flush handle and tighten with a screw if included. Turn the water valve back on and flush the toilet to test. If the flush is slow, adjust the chain to be tighter. If needed, readjust the chain by moving the metal clip up or down a few links and cut off excess chain to prevent tangling.", "time_sec": 27.241, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5046, 279, 11893, 31430, 304, 264, 26214, 11, 1156, 9311, 1007, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 13, 10783, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 553, 63702, 432, 1007, 279, 33639, 11715, 323, 1896, 700, 894, 9664, 10865, 11893, 8781, 504, 279, 11893, 6773, 13, 19242, 279, 501, 1320, 3106, 31430, 323, 4564, 279, 11893, 8781, 311, 279, 4843, 14178, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 11, 892, 374, 18093, 311, 279, 6821, 13, 5443, 625, 4813, 311, 9767, 279, 3633, 13, 22950, 279, 6437, 835, 315, 279, 11893, 6773, 1119, 279, 18198, 3705, 323, 66745, 448, 264, 21966, 421, 5230, 13, 11999, 279, 3015, 31430, 1182, 389, 323, 18198, 279, 26214, 311, 1273, 13, 1416, 279, 18198, 374, 6301, 11, 7500, 279, 8781, 311, 387, 62962, 13, 1416, 4362, 11, 1349, 4250, 279, 8781, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 2421, 7746, 323, 3931, 1007, 13623, 8781, 311, 5358, 21878, 2718, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0017, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0144, -0.0, -0.1095, -0.0002, -0.0006, -0.0048, -0.0032, -0.0, -0.6254, -0.3045, -0.0812, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.