{"id": "382", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "gt": "Passage 3 provides the necessary information to answer the question. To arrange an excel sheet alphabetically, click on the Select All button, switch to the Data tab, locate the Sort & Filter group, click on the Sort option, and then select the desired column to sort by.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps: 1. Click on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings to select all cells. 2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group. 3. Click on the Sort option. 4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. 5. Choose the column you want to sort by, such as the Product column (column B). 6. Ensure the sort order is set to A to Z for alphabetical arrangement. 7. Click on the OK button to apply the sort. The data in the spreadsheet will now be arranged alphabetically based on the selected column.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps: 1. Click on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings to select all cells. 2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group. 3. Click on the Sort option. 4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. 5. Choose the column you want to sort by, such as the Product column (column B). 6. Ensure the sort order is set to A to Z for alphabetical arrangement. 7. Click on the OK button to apply the sort. The data in the spreadsheet will now be arranged alphabetically based on the selected column.", "time_sec": 27.306, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 1795, 1493, 