{"id": "402", "question": "2006 chevy remove door panel", "gt": "To remove the door panel on a 2006 Chevy, you will need to remove the screws inside the door pull cup and one in the middle of the inside door handle. There is also a pin on the outer edge of the door that needs to be removed. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the panel off.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup and one screw in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door, there is a pin that holds the panel in place and must be removed. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the panel off the rear door. If needed, use a screwdriver to remove all screws and clips, gently pull the panel away from the frame, and disconnect any wiring connections before removing the panel completely. An instructional video is also available to guide the process.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup and one screw in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door, there is a pin that holds the panel in place and must be removed. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the panel off the rear door. If needed, use a screwdriver to remove all screws and clips, gently pull the panel away from the frame, and disconnect any wiring connections before removing the panel completely. An instructional video is also available to guide the process.", "time_sec": 23.438, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4057, 279, 14639, 6006, 6945, 304, 264, 220, 17, 15, 15, 21, 57298, 472, 17088, 11, 498, 686, 1184, 311, 4057, 279, 1378, 44922, 7407, 4766, 279, 6006, 6815, 10525, 323, 825, 21966, 