{"id": "408", "question": "how to make panko crumbs", "gt": "To make panko crumbs, preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C). Push torn pieces or chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300 degrees F for 6 to 8 minutes, shaking the sheet twice during baking. Remove from the oven and cool completely.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to make panko crumbs, first preheat the oven to 300 degrees F. Push torn pieces or chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake for 6 to 8 minutes, shaking the sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying. Remove from the oven and cool completely. Alternatively, place ingredients in a blender carafe, pulse until coarse crumbs form, spread on half sheet pans, and bake until they just begin to brown and are crisp, about 5 minutes. Cool for 15 to 20 minutes before storing in an airtight container at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to make panko crumbs, first preheat the oven to 300 degrees F. Push torn pieces or chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake for 6 to 8 minutes, shaking the sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying. Remove from the oven and cool completely. Alternatively, place ingredients in a blender carafe, pulse until coarse crumbs form, spread on half sheet pans, and bake until they just begin to brown and are crisp, about 5 minutes. Cool for 15 to 20 minutes before storing in an airtight container at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.", "time_sec": 26.486, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1281, 281, 92852, 96577, 11, 