{"id": "473", "question": "what is the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the main difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil is the process used to extract it. Refined coconut oil is extracted from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil is extracted from the flesh of the fresh coconut. Another difference is that refined coconut oil has a higher smoke point and is therefore better suited for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized and has no taste or smell, while unrefined oil retains its distinctive coconut flavor and aroma.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit and undergoes refining which removes its aroma and flavor, resulting in a neutral taste and smell. Unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from fresh coconut flesh and retains a distinct coconut aroma and mild flavor. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to unrefined coconut oil's 350 degrees F, making it more suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit and undergoes refining which removes its aroma and flavor, resulting in a neutral taste and smell. Unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from fresh coconut flesh and retains a distinct coconut aroma and mild flavor. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to unrefined coconut oil's 350 degrees F, making it more suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying.", "time_sec": 19.116, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 37191, 33457, 5590, 374, 1865, 504, 31620, 33457, 1377