{"id": "493", "question": "how can you tell who liked your tweet", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can tell who liked your tweet:\n\nPassage 1 suggests using websites such as Favotter.net and Favstar.fm to track who has favorited your tweets. These websites show you a list of users who have favorited your tweets, allowing you to see who has shown interest in your content.\n\nPassage 2 provides a step-by-step guide on how to track who favorited your tweets. According to the passage, you can use a simple web-based website to check who favorited your tweets. Once you have access to this website, you can enter your tweet's URL to view a list of users who have favorited it.\n\nPassage 3 does not provide any information on tracking who favorited your tweets. However, it does mention that you can set up your Twitter account to notify you via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.\n\nIn summary, to tell who liked your tweet, you can use websites like Favotter.net and Favstar.fm, or set up your Twitter account to notify you via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using websites like Favotter.net and Favstar.fm which track who favorites your tweets. Additionally, you can go to Twitter.com, log in, click on your Twitter name, select Settings, then click on the Notifications link to set up email alerts whenever someone favorites your tweet.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using websites like Favotter.net and Favstar.fm which track who favorites your tweets. Additionally, you can go to Twitter.com, log in, click on your Twitter name, select Settings, then click on the Notifications link to set up email alerts whenever someone favorites your tweet.", "