{"id": "589", "question": "where does 1099-patr go on 1040", "gt": "Per the IRS instructions, patronage dividends and other distributions in boxes 1,2,3, and 5 from a cooperative, which are reported in Form 1099-PATR, are reported on Schedule C, Schedule F, or Form 4835 of the Form 1040.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, Form 1099-PATR reports taxable distributions from cooperatives, and the IRS instructions state that patronage dividends and other distributions in boxes 1, 2, 3, and 5 must be reported on Schedule C, Schedule F, or Form 4835. These schedules or forms are then attached to the individual's Form 1040. Therefore, the information from Form 1099-PATR does not go directly on Form 1040 but is reported on one of the mentioned schedules or forms which are filed with the 1040.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, Form 1099-PATR reports taxable distributions from cooperatives, and the IRS instructions state that patronage dividends and other distributions in boxes 1, 2, 3, and 5 must be reported on Schedule C, Schedule F, or Form 4835. These schedules or forms are then attached to the individual's Form 1040. Therefore, the information from Form 1099-PATR does not go directly on Form 1040 but is reported on one of the mentioned schedules or forms which are filed with the 1040.", "time_sec": 22.752, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 3377, 220, 16, 15, 24, 24, 9299, 828, 49, 6682, 58353, 42685, 504, 21676, 5859, 11, 323, 279, 33383, 11221, 1584, 429, 35280, 424, 55264, 323, 1008, 42685, 304, 14697, 220, 16, 11, 220, 17, 11, 220, 18, 11, 323, 220, 20, 1969, 387, 4961, 389, 23512, 356, 11, 23512, 434, 11, 476, 3377, 220, 19, 23, 18, 20, 13, 4220, 36769, 476, 7586, 525, 1221, 12392, 311, 279, 3842, 594, 3377, 220, 16, 15, 19, 15, 13, 15277, 11, 279, 1995, 504, 3377, 220, 16, 15, 24, 24, 9299, 828, 49, 1558