{"id": "611", "question": "how to do employee schedules", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to create an employee schedule:\n\n1. Talk to a lawyer about work laws: It is important to understand the legal requirements for creating an employee schedule, including paying overtime for hours worked beyond 40 per week. Additionally, there may be other laws to consider, such as restrictions for employees under the age of 18.\n2. Use scheduling software or a simple word processing program: You can create an employee schedule using scheduling software, a simple word processing program, or even a sheet of paper. Make a list of all employees and their duties, and create a chart of work days and hours for each day.\n3. Print or send schedules to employees: Once you have created the schedule, print out copies for each employee or send them to their email accounts. Keep a master schedule for making any changes. If you are using a digital tool, you can easily edit and share the schedule with employees.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide specific instructions on how to create an employee schedule, such as setting up the schedule format, determining pay rates, or communicating the schedule to employees.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to do employee schedules, first make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform. Then, make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day. You can create the schedule using scheduling software, a word processing program, or a sheet of paper. After creating the schedule, print out copies for employees or send the schedules to their email accounts. Keep a master schedule to make any necessary changes. Microsoft Excel can be used to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing you to reuse the template as your business grows.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to do employee schedules, first make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform. Then, make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day. You can create the schedule using scheduling software, a word processing program, or a sheet of paper. After creating the schedule, print out copies for employees or send the schedules to their email accounts. Keep a master schedule to make any necessary changes. Microsoft Excel can be used to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing you to reuse the template as your business grows.", "time_sec": 20.217, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 653, 9364, 36769, 11, 1156, 1281, 264, 1140, 315, 678, 697, 8256, 323, 279, 21300, 807, 646, 2736, 13, 5005, 11, 1281, 264, 9487, 315, 279, 975, 2849, 323, 279, 4115, 369, 1817, 1899, 13, 1446, 646, 1855, 279, 9700, 1667, 37852, 3162, 11, 264, 3409, 8692, 2025, 11, 476, 264, 10834, 315, 5567, 13, 4636, 6825, 279, 9700, 11, 1173, 700, 10993, 369, 8256, 476, 3624, 279, 36769, 311, 862, 2551, 9618, 13, 13655, 264, 7341, 9700, 311, 1281, 894, 5871, 4344, 13, 5100, 21029, 646, 387, 1483, 311, 1855, 264, 975, 9700, 369, 5248, 8256, 11, 10693, 498, 311, 25978, 279, 3811, 438, 697, 2562, 27715, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0003, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0308, -0.1395, -0.0, -0.0, -0.7926, -0.2655, -0.0063, -0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0, -0.3869, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0031, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.025, -0.3146, -0.6099, -0.5759, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0012, -0.0, -0.0086, -0.0047, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0, -0.01, -0.0051, -0.0, -0.4746, -0.1954, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.314, -0.0002, 0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.2, -0.013, 0.0, 0.0, -0.006, -0.9473, -0.4481, -0.0079, -0.0006, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.3887, -0.0, -0.0011, -0.0021, -0.0, -0.0012, -0.9331, -0.5761, -0.1275, -0.0838, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0012, -0.0779, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.039, -0.2518, -0.2334, -0.0526, -0.3494, -0.0007, -0.2802, -0.1277, -0.0, -0.3143, -0.0052, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0046, -0.0432, -0.033, -0.0, -0.0149, -0.0, -0.0, -0.2659, -0.0712, -0.2014, -0.0, -0.1888, -0.0009, -0.3879, -0.0007, -0.0047, -0.0, -0.1272, -0.0003, -0.0078], "cumulative_logprob": -10.9897, "norm_logp": -0.0939, "input_len": 463, "output_tokens": 117, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 48.8, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "620", "question": "how has it technology changed the workplace", "gt": "IT technology has significantly changed the workplace in several ways. It has improved efficiency and increased productivity, as it allows for a complete shift in how time is spent in the modern workplace. The continuous evolution of technology also changes how business is conducted and the dynamics of the workplace. Over the last 10 to 15 years, technology has drastically changed attitudes and processes in the workplace. Technology has also dramatically reshaped the average American workplace, allowing employees to interact with a global market and take work on the road.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, technology has changed the workplace by increasing efficiency and productivity, transforming business dynamics, altering workplace attitudes and processes, reshaping the office environment, enabling global market interaction, and allowing employees to work remotely. Over the past 10 to 15 years, rapid technological advancements have made it possible for employees to take work on the road, moving away from traditional office settings. The modern workplace now supports more flexible and connected operations compared to the past.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, technology has changed the workplace by increasing efficiency and productivity, transforming business dynamics, altering workplace attitudes and processes, reshaping the office environment, enabling global market interaction, and allowing employees to work remotely. Over the past 10 to 15 years, rapid technological advancements have made it possible for employees to take work on the road, moving away from traditional office settings. The modern workplace now supports more flexible and connected operations compared to the past.", "time_sec": 16.904, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 5440, 702, 5497, 279, 26368, 553, 7703, 15024, 323, 25148, 11, 45790, 2562, 29195, 11, 59823, 26368, 32626, 323, 11364, 11, 63693, 14216, 279, 5163, 4573, 11, 27362, 3644, 3081, 16230, 11, 323, 10693, 8256, 311, 975, 38429, 13, 6065, 279, 3267, 220, 16, 15, 311, 220, 16, 20, 1635, 11, 11048, 29016, 82687, 614, 1865, 432, 3204, 369, 8256, 311, 1896, 975, 389, 279, 5636, 11, 7218, 3123, 504, 8606, 5163, 5003, 13, 576, 6481, 26368, 1431, 11554, 803, 18776, 323, 8433, 7525, 7707, 311, 279, 3267, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0036, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0007, -0.0001, -0.0696, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.5244, -0.5837, -0.0006, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.031, -0.125, -0.1153, -0.0466, -0.5232, -0.6479, -0.0086, -0.4769, -0.0264, -0.0001, -0.071, -0.4332, -0.0, -0.0523, -0.5016, -0.0, -0.075, -0.134, -0.3794, -0.246, -0.3133, -0.0026, -0.0583, -0.0974, -0.5634, -0.0074, -0.0119, -0.0014, -0.14, -0.5814, -0.0004, -0.3134, -0.2298, -0.0004, -0.0032, -0.0033, -0.0, -0.0019, -0.0, -0.0, -0.2173, -0.7981, -0.0465, -0.5804, -0.0005, -1.9166, -0.8839, -0.0048, -0.252, -0.3595, -0.0011, -0.2559, -0.0208, -0.4057, -0.0009, -0.0008, -0.7468, -1.4086, -0.2566, -0.0, -0.5787, -0.0215, -0.3811, -0.2699, -1.1141, -0.6153, -0.0052, -0.633, -1.2532, -1.6503, -0.1757, -0.5126, -1.5064, -0.7938, -1.2019, -0.0002, -0.3001, -0.8594, -0.1162, -0.0129], "cumulative_logprob": -27.5646, "norm_logp": -0.2871, "input_len": 466, "output_tokens": 96, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 41.03, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "630", "question": "how to guard a tall person in basketball", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how to guard a tall person in basketball:\n\n1. Stay as close as possible to the tall, skilled shooter when guarding them near the three-point line.\n2. Actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities.\n3. Keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to defend against a tall player.\n\nTherefore, to guard a tall person in basketball, it is essential to stay close to them, move quickly laterally to maintain position, and use a defensive strategy such as keeping a wedge between the basket and the offensive player.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to guard a tall person in basketball, stay as close as possible to a tall, skilled shooter near the three-point line and actively slide your feet from side to side to minimize their shot opportunities. Additionally, keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to defend effectively.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to guard a tall person in basketball, stay as close as possible to a tall, skilled shooter near the three-point line and actively slide your feet from side to side to minimize their shot opportunities. Additionally, keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to defend effectively.", "time_sec": 11.449, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 7616, 264, 16217, 1697, 304, 19240, 11, 4717, 438, 3265, 438, 3204, 311, 264, 16217, 11, 25530, 31571, 3143, 279, 2326, 16574, 1555, 323, 22040, 14983, 697, 7541, 504, 3108, 311, 3108, 311, 29337, 862, 6552, 10488, 13, 22406, 11, 2506, 264, 63685, 1948, 279, 14024, 323, 279, 15183, 2781, 311, 10505, 13444, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0012, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0044, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0