{"id": "635", "question": "similarity and difference between nervous system and endocrine system", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are the key similarities and differences between the nervous system and the endocrine system:\n\nSimilarities:\n\n* Both systems are involved in maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\n* Both systems use chemical messengers (neurotransmitters and hormones) to transmit signals.\n* Both systems have negative feedback mechanisms to regulate their function.\n\nDifferences:\n\n* The nervous system is made up of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is composed of glands.\n* Transmission of signals occurs through electrical impulses in the nervous system, while hormones are responsible for signal transmission in the endocrine system.\n* The nervous system has a continuous structure, with cells connected to each other, while the endocrine system consists of discrete organs not physically connected to each other.\n* The nervous system uses neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system relies on the circulatory system to transmit signals.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, similarities between the nervous system and endocrine system include both being devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating activities of cells, tissues, organs, and systems, and both being regulated by negative feedback mechanisms. Both systems also use chemical messengers, though their transmission and release methods differ. Differences include the nervous system being made of neuron cells and using electrochemical pulses for transmission, while the endocrine system is made of glands and uses hormones for transmission. The nervous system is continuous with interconnected cells, whereas the endocrine system consists of discrete, non-physically connected organs. The nervous system transmits signals via neurons, while the endocrine system relies on the circulatory system for signal transmission.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_qwen3_omni", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, similarities between the nervous system and endocrine system include both being devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating activities of cells, tissues, organs, and systems, and both being regulated by negative feedback mechanisms. Both systems also use chemical messengers, though their transmission and release methods differ. Differences include the nervous system being made of neuron cells and using electrochemical pulses for transmission, while the endocrine system is made of glands and uses hormones for transmission. The nervous system is continuous with interconnected cells, whereas the endocrine system consists of discrete, non-physically connected organs. The nervous system transmits signals via neurons, while the endocrine system relies on the circulatory system for signal transmission.", "time_sec": 25.361, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 42774, 1948, 279, 22596, 1849, 323, 835, 77638, 1849, 2924, 2176, 1660, 28229, 311, 20337, 2114, 535, 10718, 553, 65415, 323, 57399, 7488, 315, 7761, 11, 38781, 11, 35753, 11, 323, 5942, 11, 323, 2176, 1660, 34219, 553, 8225, 11055, 23783, 13, 11733, 5942, 1083, 990, 11483, 9435, 14886, 11, 3498, 862, 18368, 323, 4879, 5413, 1745, 13, 85797, 2924, 279, 22596, 1849, 1660, 1865, 315, 48284, 7761, 323, 1667, 24394, 30956, 65457, 369, 18368, 11, 1393, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 374, 1865, 315, 81275, 323, 5711, 43215, 369, 18368, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 19259, 448, 82316, 7761, 11, 19853, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 17167, 315, 43179, 11, 2477, 12, 41205, 2673, 8433, 35753, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 1356, 44703, 17289, 4566, 33213, 11, 1393, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 33644, 389, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 369, 8286, 18368, 13, 151645], "